[131.285148, "i", "sed -n '1,240p' docs/formats.md\n"]
[131.285455, "o", "sed -n '1,240p' docs/formats.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[131.288488, "o", "# File Format Specifications\r\n\r\n## 1. MLCK Checkpoint Format (`.mlck`)\r\n\r\nAll multi-byte integer and floating-point values are **little-endian**.\r\n\r\n### File Layout\r\n"]
[131.288588, "o", "\r\n```\r\n[Header (56 bytes)]\r\n[Tensor Block 0]\r\n[Tensor Block 1]\r\n...\r\n[Tensor Block N-1]\r\n[Metadata Section]\r\n[Provenance Section]\r\n[Signature Block]      (only if Header.Flags bit 0 is set)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Header (56 bytes)\r\n\r\n| Offset | Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|--------|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 0 | 4 | bytes | Magic | Must be `MLCK` (0x4D 0x4C 0x43 0x4B) |\r\n| 4 | 2 | uint16 | Version | Must be `1` |\r\n| 6 | 2 | uint16 | Flags | Bit 0: signed (has signature block). Bits 1-15: reserved (must be 0) |\r\n| 8 | 4 | uint32 | NumTensors | Number of tensor blocks |\r\n"]
[131.28871, "o", "| 12 | 4 | uint32 | NumMetadata | Number of metadata key-value pairs |\r\n| 16 | 8 | uint64 | MetadataOffset | Byte offset of metadata section from file start |\r\n| 24 | 8 | uint64 | ProvenanceOffset | Byte offset of provenance section from file start |\r\n| 32 | 8 | uint64 | SignatureOffset | Byte offset of signature block (0 if unsigned) |\r\n| 40 | 8 | int64 | CreationTimestamp | Unix timestamp (seconds) when checkpoint was created |\r\n| 48 | 8 | uint64 | HeaderChecksum | FNV-1a 64-bit hash of bytes [0..48) |\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Tensor Blocks\r\n\r\nTensor blocks start immediately after the header (offset 56). Each tensor block has variable length:\r\n\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 2 | uint16 | NameLen | Length of tensor name in bytes |\r\n| NameLen | bytes | Name | UTF-8 tensor name (e.g., `encoder.layer0.weight`) |\r\n| 1 | uint8 | Dtype | Data type enum (see below) |\r\n| 1 | uint8 | NumDims | Number of dimensions (1-8) |\r\n| 4 * NumDims | uint32[] | Shape | Dimension sizes |\r\n| 8 |"]
[131.28879, "o", " uint64 | DataSize | Size of raw tensor data in bytes |\r\n| DataSize | bytes | Data | Raw tensor data |\r\n| 32 | bytes | Checksum | SHA-256 hash of the Data bytes |\r\n\r\n**Dtype values:**\r\n\r\n| Value | Type | Byte size per element |\r\n|-------|------|----------------------|\r\n| 0 | float32 | 4 |\r\n| 1 | float64 | 8 |\r\n| 2 | float16 | 2 |\r\n| 3 | int32 | 4 |\r\n| 4 | int64 | 8 |\r\n| 5 | bfloat16 | 2 |\r\n\r\n**Validation**: `DataSize` must equal `product(Shape) * element_byte_size`. If it does not match, the tensor block is malformed.\r\n\r\n### 1.3 Metadata Section\r\n\r\nLocated at `MetadataOffset`. Contains `NumMetadata` key-value pairs:\r\n\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 2 | uint16 | KeyLen | Length of key |\r\n"]
[131.288855, "o", "| KeyLen | bytes | Key | UTF-8 key string |\r\n| 4 | uint32 | ValueLen | Length of value |\r\n| ValueLen | bytes | Value | UTF-8 value (JSON-encoded) |\r\n\r\nCommon metadata keys:\r\n- `model_name`: string, the model architecture name\r\n- `dataset`: string, training dataset identifier\r\n- `training_config`: JSON object with hyperparameters\r\n- `notes`: string, free-form notes\r\n\r\n### 1.4 Provenance Section\r\n\r\n"]
[131.288918, "o", "Located at `ProvenanceOffset`. Fixed structure followed by variable-length fields:\r\n\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 40 | bytes | GitCommit | ASCII hex string of git commit hash (zero-padded if absent) |\r\n| 32 | bytes | DatasetHash | Raw SHA-256 of the training dataset manifest |\r\n| 32 | bytes | ConfigHash | Raw SHA-256 of the training configuration |\r\n| 8 | int64 | TrainingTimestamp | Unix timestamp when training started |\r\n| 8 | float64 | TrainingDuration | Training duration in seconds |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | FrameworkLen | Length of framework name |\r\n| FrameworkLen | bytes | Framework | UTF-8 framework name (e.g., `PyTorch`, `JAX`) |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | FrameworkVersionLen | Length of framework version string |\r\n"]
[131.288996, "o", "| FrameworkVersionLen | bytes | FrameworkVersion | UTF-8 version (e.g., `2.1.0`) |\r\n| 4 | uint32 | Epoch | Training epoch at checkpoint time |\r\n| 8 | uint64 | GlobalStep | Global training step |\r\n| 8 | float64 | LearningRate | Learning rate at checkpoint time |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | ParentHashLen | Length of parent hash string (0 = no parent) |\r\n| ParentHashLen | bytes | ParentHash | ASCII hex SHA-256 of the parent checkpoint file (for lineage) |\r\n\r\n### 1.5 Signature Block\r\n\r\n"]
[131.289058, "o", "Located at `SignatureOffset` (only present if `Flags` bit 0 is set):\r\n\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 1 | uint8 | Algorithm | 0 = HMAC-SHA256 |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | SignerIdLen | Length of signer identifier |\r\n| SignerIdLen | bytes | SignerId | UTF-8 signer identifier (used as HMAC key) |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | SignatureLen | Length of signature |\r\n| SignatureLen | bytes | Signature | The signature bytes |\r\n\r\n"]
[131.289118, "o", "**HMAC-SHA256 computation**: The HMAC is computed over all bytes from offset 0 to `SignatureOffset` (exclusive), using `SignerId` as the HMAC key.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Training Log Shard Format (`.jsonl`)\r\n\r\nEach `.jsonl` file contains one JSON object per line. Each object represents a training step event:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\",\r\n  \"epoch\": 1,\r\n"]
[131.289181, "o", "  \"step\": 1000,\r\n  \"loss\": 0.5234,\r\n  \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n  \"grad_norm\": 1.23,\r\n  \"acc\": 0.8200,\r\n  \"event\": \"step\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Required Fields\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Description |\r\n|-------|------|-------------|\r\n| `ts` | string | ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC, `Z` suffix required) |\r\n"]
[131.289272, "o", "| `epoch` | integer | Current training epoch (0-indexed) |\r\n| `step` | integer | Global training step (monotonically increasing within an epoch) |\r\n\r\n### Optional Metric Fields\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Description |\r\n|-------|------|-------------|\r\n| `loss` | float | Training loss |\r\n| `lr` | float | Learning rate |\r\n| `grad_norm` | float | Gradient L2 norm |\r\n| `acc` | float | Accuracy metric (0.0 to 1.0) |\r\n| `event` | string | Event type: `step`, `epoch_end`, `checkpoint`, `eval` |\r\n\r\n### Shard Semantics\r\n\r\n- Multiple shard files may exist in the same evidence directory\r\n- Shards may have overlapping `(epoch, step)` ranges\r\n- Shards are named arbitrarily (any `.jsonl` filename is valid)\r\n"]
[131.289343, "o", "- Lines within a single shard are not guaranteed to be in chronological order\r\n- Malformed lines (invalid JSON) should be silently skipped with a count in verbose output\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. Configuration File Format (`config_*.json`)\r\n\r\nTraining configuration files follow the naming pattern `config_*.json`:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n  \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\",\r\n  \"batch_size\": 256,\r\n  \"learning_rate\": 0.1,\r\n  \"lr_schedule\": \"cosine\",\r\n  \"weight_decay\": 0.0001,\r\n"]
[131.289404, "o", "  \"epochs\": 90,\r\n  \"optimizer\": \"sgd\",\r\n  \"momentum\": 0.9,\r\n  \"seed\": 42\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese files are used by the anomaly detector to cross-reference declared hyperparameters with observed training behavior.\r\n"]
[131.289895, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[131.28998, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[131.619127, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' docs/analysis_rules.md\n"]
[131.619463, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' docs/analysis_rules.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[131.622634, "o", "# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n\r\n## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n\r\n"]
[131.622717, "o", "Given multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n\r\n1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **latest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n\r\nAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files containe"]
[131.622814, "o", "d this `(epoch, step)`\r\n- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n\r\nAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n\r\n### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n\r\n- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n\r\n### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n\r\n- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n"]
[131.622882, "o", "- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n\r\n### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n"]
[131.623033, "o", "\r\n### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n\r\n- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n\r\n"]
[131.623116, "o", "### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n\r\n### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n\r\n### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n\r\n"]
[131.623184, "o", "### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\n- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n\r\n### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n- **Severity**: `low`\r\n- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n\r\n### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n"]
[131.623255, "o", "## 3. Query Language\r\n\r\n### 3.1 Grammar\r\n\r\n```\r\nquery      := condition (BOOL_OP condition)*\r\ncondition  := field COMP_OP value\r\nBOOL_OP    := \"AND\" | \"OR\"\r\nCOMP_OP    := \">\" | \"<\" | \">=\" | \"<=\" | \"==\" | \"!=\"\r\nfield      := \"step\" | \"epoch\" | \"loss\" | \"lr\" | \"grad_norm\" | \"acc\" | \"event\" | \"ts\"\r\nvalue      := NUMBER | QUOTED_STRING | TIMESTAMP\r\nNUMBER     := integer or float literal\r\nQUOTED_STRING := '\"' ... '\"' (double-quoted string)\r\nTIMESTAMP  := ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 3.2 Operator Precedence\r\n"]
[131.623326, "o", "\r\n- `AND` binds tighter than `OR`\r\n- Parentheses are NOT supported (keep the grammar simple)\r\n- Evaluation: left to right with AND having higher precedence\r\n\r\nExample: `loss > 1.0 OR grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3`\r\nParses as: `loss > 1.0 OR (grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3)`\r\n\r\n### 3.3 Type Rules\r\n\r\n- `step`, `epoch`: integer comparisons\r\n- `loss`, `lr`, `grad_norm`, `acc`: float comparisons (tolerance 1e-9 for `==`)\r\n- `event`: string comparisons (`==`, `!=` only)\r\n- `ts`: timestamp comparisons (parse both sides as time, compare chronologically)\r\n"]
[131.623387, "o", "\r\n### 3.4 Output\r\n\r\nJSON array of matching timeline entries (after reconstruction), sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n\r\n### 3.5 Error Handling\r\n\r\n- Invalid query syntax: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n- Unknown field name: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n- Type mismatch (e.g., `event > 5`): exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Lineage Graph Construction\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Node Identification"]
[131.623462, "o", "\r\n\r\nEach `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Edge Construction\r\n\r\nFor each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:\r\n- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.\r\n- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classified as an **orphan**.\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Graph Validation\r\n\r\n- The lineage graph must be a DAG. If a cycle is detected, report each cycle's member nodes.\r\n- Roots: nodes with no incoming edges and empty `ParentHash`.\r\n- Leaves: nodes with no outgoing edges.\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Topological Sort\r\n\r\n"]
[131.623512, "o", "The lineage output includes a topological ordering of all non-orphan nodes, from root to leaf. If multiple valid orderings exist, sort by `CreationTimestamp` ascending as tiebreaker.\r\n"]
[131.624006, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[131.624066, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[131.906491, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' docs/output_schema.md\n"]
[131.906819, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' docs/output_schema.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[131.909909, "o", "# Output Schemas\r\n\r\nAll commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Ingest Output\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n"]
[131.910038, "o", "  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\r\n  \"artifacts\": {\r\n    \"checkpoints\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n        \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n        \"version\": 1,\r\n        \"num_tensors\": 12,\r\n        \"num_metadata\": 3,\r\n        \"signed\": false,\r\n        \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n        \"provenance\": {\r\n          \"epoch\": 1,\r\n          \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n          \"framework\": \"PyTorch\",\r\n          \"framework_version\": \"2.1.0\",\r\n          \"parent_hash\": \"\"\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"log_shards\": [\r\n"]
[131.910145, "o", "      {\r\n        \"file\": \"shard_001.jsonl\",\r\n        \"entries\": 500,\r\n        \"step_range\": [0, 5000],\r\n        \"epoch_range\": [0, 1],\r\n        \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\"]\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"configs\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"file\": \"config_train.json\",\r\n        \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n"]
[131.91025, "o", "        \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\"\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  \"totals\": {\r\n    \"checkpoints\": 3,\r\n    \"log_shards\": 4,\r\n    \"configs\": 1\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `file_hash`: SHA-256 hex of the entire `.mlck` file content.\r\n- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n- `log_shards` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n- `configs` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n- `step_range`: `[min_step, max_step]` across all entries in the shard.\r\n- `epoch_range`: `[min_epoch, max_epoch]` across all entries.\r\n- `time_range`: `[earliest_ts, latest_ts]` as ISO 8601 strings.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Timeline Output\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"total_entries\": 1200,\r\n  \"total_epochs\": 5,\r\n  \"step_range\": [0, 50000],\r\n"]
[131.910326, "o", "  \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-17T14:00:00Z\"],\r\n  \"conflicts_resolved\": 3,\r\n  \"gaps\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"after_step\": 5000,\r\n      \"before_step\": 5200,\r\n      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n      \"gap_steps\": 200,\r\n      \"after_ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n      \"before_ts\": \"2024-01-15T13:00:00Z\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"entries\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\",\r\n      \"epoch\": 0,\r\n      \"step\": 0,\r\n      \"loss\": 6.9078,\r\n      \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n"]
[131.910412, "o", "      \"grad_norm\": 12.34,\r\n      \"acc\": 0.001,\r\n      \"event\": \"step\",\r\n      \"sources\": [\"shard_001.jsonl\"],\r\n      \"conflict\": false\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `entries`: sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n- `sources`: list of shard filenames (basenames) that contained this `(epoch, step)`.\r\n- `conflict`: `true` if this entry was chosen by conflict resolution.\r\n- `gaps`: only gaps where `gap_steps > 100` within the same epoch.\r\n- Entries with missing optional fields omit them from the JSON (do not include null).\r\n\r\n---\r\n"]
[131.910509, "o", "\r\n## 3. Verify Output\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"checkpoints\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n      \"valid\": true,\r\n      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": true,\r\n      \"signature_valid\": null,\r\n      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n      \"issues\": []\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n      \"valid\": false,\r\n      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": false,\r\n      \"signature_valid\": true,\r\n"]
[131.910592, "o", "      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n      \"issues\": [\r\n        \"tensor_checksum_mismatch:encoder.layer2.weight\"\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"total\": 3,\r\n    \"valid\": 2,\r\n    \"invalid\": 1\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\n"]
[131.91064, "o", "- `issues`: list of human-readable issue descriptions. Format for tensor checksum mismatch: `\"tensor_checksum_mismatch:<tensor_name>\"`.\r\n- `valid`: `true` only if all applicable checks pass.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Detect Output\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"anomalies\": [\r\n    {\r\n"]
[131.91068, "o", "      \"id\": \"ANOM-001\",\r\n      \"type\": \"gradient_spike\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\n      \"epoch\": 2,\r\n      \"step\": 3456,\r\n      \"details\": {\r\n        \"observed\": 15.3,\r\n"]
[131.910814, "o", "        \"window_mean\": 1.2,\r\n        \"window_stddev\": 0.3,\r\n        \"z_score\": 47.0\r\n      },\r\n      \"source\": \"shard_002.jsonl\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"ANOM-002\",\r\n      \"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\n      \"details\": {\r\n        \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n        \"tensor_name\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\",\r\n        \"expected_checksum\": \"abcd1234...\",\r\n        \"actual_checksum\": \"efgh5678...\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"source\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"total\": 5,\r\n    \"by_severity\": {\r\n      \"critical\": 1,\r\n      \"high\": 2,\r\n      \"medium\": 1,\r\n      \"low\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"by_type\": {\r\n      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n"]
[131.910864, "o", "      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\r\n"]
[131.911071, "o", "- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n- `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.\r\n- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\r\n- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 5. Lineage Output\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"nodes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n      \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n"]
[131.911161, "o", "      \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n      \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n      \"parent_hash\": \"\",\r\n      \"is_root\": true,\r\n      \"is_leaf\": false,\r\n      \"is_orphan\": false\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"edges\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"from\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n      \"to\": \"d4e5f6...\",\r\n      \"from_file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n      \"to_file\": \"model_epoch2.mlck\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"roots\": [\"a1b2c3...\"],\r\n  \"leaves\": [\"g7h8i9...\"],\r\n  \"orphans\": [],\r\n  \"topological_order\": [\"a1b2c3...\", \"d4e5f6...\", \"g7h8i9...\"],\r\n  \"cycles\": []\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `nodes`: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n- `edges`: sorted by `from` hash then `to` hash lexicographically.\r\n- `roots`: file hashes of root nodes (no parent), sorted.\r\n- `leaves`: file hashes of leaf nodes (no children), sorted.\r\n- `orphans`: file hashes of orphan nodes (parent not found), sorted.\r\n- `topological_order`: valid topological sort of non-orphan nodes, ties broken by `creation_timestamp`.\r\n"]
[131.91161, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
