[142.699103, "i", "sed -n '221,440p' docs/formats.md\n"]
[142.699422, "o", "sed -n '221,440p' docs/formats.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[142.702784, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[142.993609, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' docs/analysis_rules.md\n"]
[142.994127, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' docs/analysis_rules.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[142.997468, "o", "# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n\r\n## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n\r\nGiven multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n\r\n1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n"]
[142.997569, "o", "2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **latest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n\r\nAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n\r\n"]
[142.997658, "o", "Anomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n\r\n### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n\r\n- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n\r\n### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n\r\n- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n"]
[142.99773, "o", "- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n\r\n### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n\r\n### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n\r\n"]
[142.997805, "o", "- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n\r\n### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n\r\n### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n"]
[142.997888, "o", "- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n\r\n### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n\r\n### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set"]
[142.998011, "o", "\r\n- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n\r\n### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n- **Severity**: `low`\r\n- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n\r\n### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n\r\n---\r\n"]
[142.998085, "o", "\r\n## 3. Query Language\r\n\r\n### 3.1 Grammar\r\n\r\n```\r\nquery      := condition (BOOL_OP condition)*\r\ncondition  := field COMP_OP value\r\nBOOL_OP    := \"AND\" | \"OR\"\r\nCOMP_OP    := \">\" | \"<\" | \">=\" | \"<=\" | \"==\" | \"!=\"\r\nfield      := \"step\" | \"epoch\" | \"loss\" | \"lr\" | \"grad_norm\" | \"acc\" | \"event\" | \"ts\"\r\nvalue      := NUMBER | QUOTED_STRING | TIMESTAMP\r\nNUMBER     := integer or float literal\r\nQUOTED_STRING := '\"' ... '\"' (double-quoted string)\r\nTIMESTAMP  := ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z)\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[142.998153, "o", "### 3.2 Operator Precedence\r\n\r\n- `AND` binds tighter than `OR`\r\n- Parentheses are NOT supported (keep the grammar simple)\r\n- Evaluation: left to right with AND having higher precedence\r\n\r\nExample: `loss > 1.0 OR grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3`\r\nParses as: `loss > 1.0 OR (grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3)`\r\n\r\n### 3.3 Type Rules\r\n\r\n- `step`, `epoch`: integer comparisons\r\n"]
[142.998228, "o", "- `loss`, `lr`, `grad_norm`, `acc`: float comparisons (tolerance 1e-9 for `==`)\r\n- `event`: string comparisons (`==`, `!=` only)\r\n- `ts`: timestamp comparisons (parse both sides as time, compare chronologically)\r\n\r\n### 3.4 Output\r\n\r\nJSON array of matching timeline entries (after reconstruction), sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n\r\n### 3.5 Error Handling\r\n\r\n- Invalid query syntax: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n- Unknown field name: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n- Type mismatch (e.g., `event > 5`): exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n"]
[142.998302, "o", "## 4. Lineage Graph Construction\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Node Identification\r\n\r\nEach `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Edge Construction\r\n\r\nFor each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:\r\n"]
[142.998371, "o", "- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.\r\n- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classified as an **orphan**.\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Graph Validation\r\n\r\n- The lineage graph must be a DAG. If a cycle is detected, report each cycle's member nodes.\r\n- Roots: nodes with no incoming edges and empty `ParentHash`.\r\n- Leaves: nodes with no outgoing edges.\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Topological Sort\r\n\r\nThe lineage output includes a topological ordering of all non-orphan nodes, from root to leaf. If multiple valid orderings exist, sort by `CreationTimestamp` ascending as tiebreaker.\r\n"]
[142.998855, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
