[167.517904, "o", "# mlforge - ML Model Artifact Forensics Engine\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n"]
[167.517955, "o", "`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\n\r\n## CLI Interface\r\n\r\nThe binary is built as `mlforge` and placed at `/app/mlforge` (or on `$PATH` after `go install`).\r\n\r\n```\r\nmlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [flags]\r\n"]
[167.518101, "o", "```\r\n\r\n### Commands\r\n\r\n| Command | Description |\r\n|---------|-------------|\r\n| `ingest` | Scan evidence directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n| `lineage` | Build and output model lineage DAG |\r\n| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n| `report` | Generate full forensic report combining all analyses |\r\n\r\n### Global Flags\r\n\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json` or `text` |\r\n| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n\r\n### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n\r\n#### `ingest`\r\n"]
[167.518178, "o", "\r\nScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n"]
[167.518258, "o", "\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n\r\nIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n\r\n#### `timeline`\r\n\r\nParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n\r\n**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `verify`\r\n\r\nFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n"]
[167.518347, "o", "1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)\r\n2. Validate the header checksum\r\n3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `detect`\r\n\r\nRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `lineage`\r\n\r\n"]
[167.518429, "o", "Build a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n\r\n**Rules**:\r\n- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n- Root nodes have empty `parent_hash`\r\n- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the evidence set\r\n- If a cycle is detected, report it as an anomaly (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `query`\r\n\r\n```\r\nmlforge query <evidence-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[167.518492, "o", "Filter the unified timeline using the query expression language defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Query Language\".\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n\r\n#### `report`\r\n\r\nGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results.\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n\r\n## Exit Codes\r\n"]
[167.518569, "o", "\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| 0 | Success |\r\n| 1 | Input error (missing directory, no artifacts, invalid arguments) |\r\n| 2 | Parse error (corrupt or unreadable artifact) |\r\n\r\nWhen a parse error occurs for individual artifacts within a batch operation (e.g., one corrupt checkpoint among several), the tool should continue processing remaining artifacts, report the error in the output, and exit with code 0. Exit code 2 is only for cases where the error prevents any meaningful output.\r\n\r\n## Build\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd /app && go build -o mlforge ./cmd/mlforge\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Cross-References\r\n\r\n"]
[167.51862, "o", "- Binary formats: `/app/docs/formats.md`\r\n- Detection algorithms and query language: `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`\r\n- JSON output schemas: `/app/docs/output_schema.md`\r\n"]
