[175.110396, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' docs/spec.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[175.113407, "o", "# mlforge - ML Model Artifact Forensics Engine\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n"]
[175.113507, "o", "`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\n\r\n## CLI Interface\r\n\r\nThe binary is built as `mlforge` and placed at `/app/mlforge` (or on `$PATH` after `go install`).\r\n\r\n```\r\nmlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Commands\r\n\r\n| Command | Description |\r\n|---------|-------------|\r\n| `ingest` | Scan evidence directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n| `lineage` | Build and output model lineage DAG |\r\n| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n| `report` | Generate full forensic"]
[175.113611, "o", " report combining all analyses |\r\n\r\n### Global Flags\r\n\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json` or `text` |\r\n| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n\r\n### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n\r\n#### `ingest`\r\n\r\nScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n\r\nIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n\r\n#### `timeline`\r\n\r\nParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n\r\n"]
[175.113677, "o", "**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `verify`\r\n\r\nFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)\r\n2. Validate the header checksum\r\n3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n"]
[175.113763, "o", "4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `detect`\r\n\r\nRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `lineage`\r\n\r\nBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n\r\n"]
[175.113826, "o", "**Rules**:\r\n- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n- Root nodes have empty `parent_hash`\r\n- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the evidence set\r\n- If a cycle is detected, report it as an anomaly (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `query`\r\n\r\n```\r\nmlforge query <evidence-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[175.11389, "o", "Filter the unified timeline using the query expression language defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Query Language\".\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n\r\n#### `report`\r\n\r\nGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results.\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n\r\n## Exit Codes\r\n\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| 0 | Success |\r\n"]
[175.113995, "o", "| 1 | Input error (missing directory, no artifacts, invalid arguments) |\r\n| 2 | Parse error (corrupt or unreadable artifact) |\r\n\r\nWhen a parse error occurs for individual artifacts within a batch operation (e.g., one corrupt checkpoint among several), the tool should continue processing remaining artifacts, report the error in the output, and exit with code 0. Exit code 2 is only for cases where the error prevents any meaningful output.\r\n\r\n## Build\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd /app && go build -o mlforge ./cmd/mlforge\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Cross-References\r\n\r\n- Binary formats: `/app/docs/formats.md`\r\n- Detection algorithms and query language: `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`\r\n- JSON output schemas: `/app/docs/output_schema.md`\r\n"]
[175.114507, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[175.114568, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[189.270875, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' docs/formats.md\n"]
[189.271203, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' docs/formats.md\r\n"]
[189.271302, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[189.27409, "o", "# File Format Specifications\r\n\r\n## 1. MLCK Checkpoint Format (`.mlck`)\r\n\r\nAll multi-byte integer and floating-point values are **little-endian**.\r\n\r\n### File Layout\r\n"]
[189.274213, "o", "\r\n```\r\n[Header (56 bytes)]\r\n[Tensor Block 0]\r\n[Tensor Block 1]\r\n...\r\n[Tensor Block N-1]\r\n[Metadata Section]\r\n[Provenance Section]\r\n[Signature Block]      (only if Header.Flags bit 0 is set)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Header (56 bytes)\r\n\r\n| Offset | Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|--------|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 0 | 4 | bytes | Magic | Must be `MLCK` (0x4D 0x4C 0x43 0x4B) |\r\n| 4 | 2 | uint16 | Version | Must be `1` |\r\n| 6 | 2 | uint16 | Flags | Bit 0: signed (has signature block). Bits 1-15: reserved (must be 0) |\r\n| 8 | 4 | uint32 | NumTensors | Number of tensor blocks |\r\n| 12 | 4 | uint32 | NumMetadata | Number of metadata key-value pairs |\r\n| 16 | 8 | uint64 | MetadataOffset | Byte offset of metadata section from file start |\r\n| 24 | 8 | uint64 | ProvenanceOffset | Byte offset of provenance section from file start |\r\n"]
[189.274309, "o", "| 32 | 8 | uint64 | SignatureOffset | Byte offset of signature block (0 if unsigned) |\r\n| 40 | 8 | int64 | CreationTimestamp | Unix timestamp (seconds) when checkpoint was created |\r\n| 48 | 8 | uint64 | HeaderChecksum | FNV-1a 64-bit hash of bytes [0..48) |\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Tensor Blocks\r\n\r\nTensor blocks start immediately after the header (offset 56). Each tensor block has variable length:\r\n"]
[189.274436, "o", "\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 2 | uint16 | NameLen | Length of tensor name in bytes |\r\n| NameLen | bytes | Name | UTF-8 tensor name (e.g., `encoder.layer0.weight`) |\r\n| 1 | uint8 | Dtype | Data type enum (see below) |\r\n| 1 | uint8 | NumDims | Number of dimensions (1-8) |\r\n| 4 * NumDims | uint32[] | Shape | Dimension sizes |\r\n| 8 | uint64 | DataSize | Size of raw tensor data in bytes |\r\n| DataSize | bytes | Data | Raw tensor data |\r\n| 32 | bytes | Checksum | SHA-256 hash of the Data bytes |\r\n\r\n**Dtype values:**\r\n\r\n| Value | Type | Byte size per element |\r\n|-------|------|----------------------|\r\n| 0 | float32 | 4 |\r\n| 1 | float64 | 8 |\r\n| 2 | float16 | 2 |\r\n| 3 | int32 | 4 |\r\n| 4 | int64 | 8 |\r\n| 5 | bfloat16 | 2 |\r\n\r\n**Validation**: `DataSize` must equal `product(Shape) * element_byte_size`. If it does not match, the tensor block is malformed.\r\n\r\n### 1.3 Metadata Section\r\n\r\nLocated at `MetadataOffset`. Contains `NumMetadata` key-value pairs:\r\n\r\n| Size | Type"]
[189.274544, "o", " | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 2 | uint16 | KeyLen | Length of key |\r\n| KeyLen | bytes | Key | UTF-8 key string |\r\n| 4 | uint32 | ValueLen | Length of value |\r\n| ValueLen | bytes | Value | UTF-8 value (JSON-encoded) |\r\n\r\nCommon metadata keys:\r\n- `model_name`: string, the model architecture name\r\n- `dataset`: string, training dataset identifier\r\n- `training_config`: JSON object with hyperparameters\r\n- `notes`: string, free-form notes\r\n\r\n### 1.4 Provenance Section\r\n\r\nLocated at `ProvenanceOffset`. Fixed structure followed by variable-length fields:\r\n\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 40 | bytes | GitCommit | ASCII hex string of git commit hash (zero-padded if absent) |\r\n| 32 | bytes | DatasetHash | Raw SHA-256 of the training dataset manifest |\r\n| 32 | bytes | ConfigHash | Raw SHA-256 of the training configuration |\r\n| 8 | int64 | TrainingTimestamp | Unix timestamp when training started |\r\n| 8 | float64 | TrainingDuration | Train"]
[189.274638, "o", "ing duration in seconds |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | FrameworkLen | Length of framework name |\r\n| FrameworkLen | bytes | Framework | UTF-8 framework name (e.g., `PyTorch`, `JAX`) |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | FrameworkVersionLen | Length of framework version string |\r\n| FrameworkVersionLen | bytes | FrameworkVersion | UTF-8 version (e.g., `2.1.0`) |\r\n| 4 | uint32 | Epoch | Training epoch at checkpoint time |\r\n| 8 | uint64 | GlobalStep | Global training step |\r\n| 8 | float64 | LearningRate | Learning rate at checkpoint time |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | ParentHashLen | Length of parent hash string (0 = no parent) |\r\n| ParentHashLen | bytes | ParentHash | ASCII hex SHA-256 of the parent checkpoint file (for lineage) |\r\n\r\n### 1.5 Signature Block\r\n\r\nLocated at `SignatureOffset` (only present if `Flags` bit 0 is set):\r\n\r\n| Size | Type | Field | Description |\r\n|------|------|-------|-------------|\r\n| 1 | uint8 | Algorithm | 0 = HMAC-SHA256 |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | SignerIdLen | Length of signer identifier |\r\n| SignerIdLen | bytes | SignerId | UTF-8 signer "]
[189.274893, "o", "identifier (used as HMAC key) |\r\n| 2 | uint16 | SignatureLen | Length of signature |\r\n| SignatureLen | bytes | Signature | The signature bytes |\r\n\r\n**HMAC-SHA256 computation**: The HMAC is computed over all bytes from offset 0 to `SignatureOffset` (exclusive), using `SignerId` as the HMAC key.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Training Log Shard Format (`.jsonl`)\r\n\r\nEach `.jsonl` file contains one JSON object per line. Each object represents a training step event:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\",\r\n  \"epoch\": 1,\r\n  \"step\": 1000,\r\n  \"loss\": 0.5234,\r\n  \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n  \"grad_norm\": 1.23,\r\n  \"acc\": 0.8200,\r\n  \"event\": \"step\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Required Fields\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Description |\r\n|-------|------|-------------|\r\n| `ts` | string | ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC, `Z` suffix required) |\r\n| `epoch` | integer | Current training epoch (0-indexed) |\r\n| `step` | integer | Global training step (monotonically increasing within an epoch) |\r\n\r\n### Optional Metric Fields\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Description |\r\n|-------|------|-------"]
[189.275023, "o", "------|\r\n| `loss` | float | Training loss |\r\n| `lr` | float | Learning rate |\r\n| `grad_norm` | float | Gradient L2 norm |\r\n| `acc` | float | Accuracy metric (0.0 to 1.0) |\r\n| `event` | string | Event type: `step`, `epoch_end`, `checkpoint`, `eval` |\r\n\r\n### Shard Semantics\r\n\r\n- Multiple shard files may exist in the same evidence directory\r\n- Shards may have overlapping `(epoch, step)` ranges\r\n- Shards are named arbitrarily (any `.jsonl` filename is valid)\r\n- Lines within a single shard are not guaranteed to be in chronological order\r\n- Malformed lines (invalid JSON) should be silently skipped with a count in verbose output\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. Configuration File Format (`config_*.json`)\r\n\r\nTraining configuration files follow the naming pattern `config_*.json`:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n  \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\",\r\n  \"batch_size\": 256,\r\n  \"learning_rate\": 0.1,\r\n  \"lr_schedule\": \"cosine\",\r\n  \"weight_decay\": 0.0001,\r\n  \"epochs\": 90,\r\n  \"optimizer\": \"sgd\",\r\n  \"momentum\": 0.9,\r\n  \"seed\": 42\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[189.275109, "o", "These files are used by the anomaly detector to cross-reference declared hyperparameters with observed training behavior.\r\n"]
[189.275525, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
