[232.413209, "i", "printf '=== analysis 1-90 ===\\n'; nl -ba docs/analysis_rules.md | sed -n '1,90p'\n"]
[232.413778, "o", "printf '=== analysis 1-90 ===\\n'; nl -ba docs/analysis_rules.md | sed -n '1,90p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[232.413912, "o", "=== analysis 1-90 ===\r\n"]
[232.417684, "o", "     1\t# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n     4\t\r\n     5"]
[232.417809, "o", "\t### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\tGiven multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n    10\t2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n    11\t   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n    12\t   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **latest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n    13\t3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n    14\t4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n    15\t   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n    16\t   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n"]
[232.417907, "o", "    19\t\r\n    20\tAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n    21\t- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n    22\t- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n    23\t- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t---\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n    28\t\r\n    29"]
[232.417993, "o", "\tAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    34\t- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n    35\t- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n    36\t- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n"]
[232.418053, "o", "    37\t- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n    38\t- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n    41\t\r\n"]
[232.418112, "o", "    42\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    43\t- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n    44\t- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n    45\t- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n    46\t- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n    47\t- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t"]
[232.418175, "o", "### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n    52\t- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n    53\t  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n    54\t  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n    55\t- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n"]
[232.418234, "o", "    56\t- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n    61\t- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n    62\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n"]
[232.4183, "o", "    63\t- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n    68\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    69\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    70\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    71\t\r\n    72\t### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n"]
[232.41836, "o", "    73\t\r\n    74\t- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n    75\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    76\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    77\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n"]
[232.418423, "o", "    78\t\r\n    79\t### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\t- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n    82\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    83\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    84\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n"]
[232.41848, "o", "    85\t\r\n    86\t### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\n    89\t- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n    90\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n"]
[232.419121, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[232.419186, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[236.487772, "i", "printf '=== analysis 91-173 ===\\n'; nl -ba docs/analysis_rules.md | sed -n '91,173p'\n"]
[236.488401, "o", "printf '=== analysis 91-173 ===\\n'; nl -ba docs/analysis_rules.md | sed -n '91,173p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[236.488513, "o", "=== analysis 91-173 ===\r\n"]
[236.492279, "o", "    91\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n    94\t\r\n    95\t- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n"]
[236.492391, "o", "    96\t- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n    97\t- **Severity**: `low`\r\n    98\t- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n    99\t\r\n   100\t### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n"]
[236.492471, "o", "   101\t\r\n   102\t- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n   103\t- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n   104\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n   105\t- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n   106\t\r\n   107\t---\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t## 3. Query Language\r\n   110\t\r\n   111\t### 3.1 Grammar\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t```\r\n   114\tquery      := condition (BOOL_OP condition)*\r\n"]
[236.492589, "o", "   115\tcondition  := field COMP_OP value\r\n   116\tBOOL_OP    := \"AND\" | \"OR\"\r\n   117\tCOMP_OP    := \">\" | \"<\" | \">=\" | \"<=\" | \"==\" | \"!=\"\r\n   118\tfield      := \"step\" | \"epoch\" | \"loss\" | \"lr\" | \"grad_norm\" | \"acc\" | \"event\" | \"ts\"\r\n   119\tvalue      := NUMBER | QUOTED_STRING | TIMESTAMP\r\n   120\tNUMBER     := integer or float literal\r\n   121\tQUOTED_STRING := '\"' ... '\"' (double-quoted string)\r\n   122\tTIMESTAMP  := ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z)\r\n   123\t```\r\n   124\t\r\n   125\t### 3.2 Operator Precedence\r\n   126\t\r\n   127\t- `AND` binds tighter than `OR`\r\n   128\t- Parentheses are NOT supported (keep the grammar simple)\r\n   129\t- Evaluation: left to right with AND having higher precedence\r\n   130\t\r\n   131\tExample: `loss > 1.0 OR grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3`\r\n   132\tParses as: `loss > 1.0 OR (grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3)`\r\n   133\t\r\n   134\t### 3.3 Type Rules\r\n   135\t\r\n   136\t- `step`, `epoch`: integer comparisons\r\n   137\t- `loss`, `lr`, `grad_norm`, `acc`: float comparisons (tolerance 1e-9 for `==`)\r"]
[236.492664, "o", "\n   138\t- `event`: string comparisons (`==`, `!=` only)\r\n   139\t- `ts`: timestamp comparisons (parse both sides as time, compare chronologically)\r\n   140\t\r\n   141\t### 3.4 Output\r\n   142\t\r\n   143\tJSON array of matching timeline entries (after reconstruction), sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   144\t\r\n   145\t### 3.5 Error Handling\r\n   146\t\r\n   147\t- Invalid query syntax: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   148\t- Unknown field name: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   149\t- Type mismatch (e.g., `event > 5`): exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   150\t\r\n"]
[236.492743, "o", "   151\t---\r\n   152\t\r\n   153\t## 4. Lineage Graph Construction\r\n   154\t\r\n   155\t### 4.1 Node Identification\r\n   156\t\r\n   157\tEach `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t### 4.2 Edge Construction\r\n   160\t\r\n   161\tFor each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:\r\n"]
[236.492806, "o", "   162\t- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.\r\n   163\t- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classified as an **orphan**.\r\n   164\t\r\n   165\t### 4.3 Graph Validation\r\n   166\t\r\n   167\t- The lineage graph must be a DAG. If a cycle is detected, report each cycle's member nodes.\r\n   168\t- Roots: nodes with no incoming edges and empty `ParentHash`.\r\n   169\t- Leaves: nodes with no outgoing edges.\r\n   170\t\r\n   171\t### 4.4 Topological Sort\r\n   172\t\r\n"]
[236.492868, "o", "   173\tThe lineage output includes a topological ordering of all non-orphan nodes, from root to leaf. If multiple valid orderings exist, sort by `CreationTimestamp` ascending as tiebreaker.\r\n"]
[236.49341, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[236.493438, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
