[1875.675313, "o", "cs.go:278:\t\tvc := verifyCheckpoint(p)\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:279:\t\tout.Checkpoints = append(out.Checkpoints, vc)\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:281:\tsort.Slice(out.Checkpoints, func(i, j int) bool {\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:282:\t\treturn out.Checkpoints[i].File < out.Checkpoints[j].File\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:284:\tout.Summary.Total = len(out.Checkpoints)\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:285:\tfor _, c := range out.Checkpoints {\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:295:func verifyCheckpoint(path string) VerifyCheckpoint {\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:296:\tvc := VerifyCheckpoint{\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:300:\tcf, err := checkpoint.Parse(path)\r\ninternal/forensics/forensics.go:369:func validateProvenance(cf *types.CheckpointFile) bool {\r\ndocs/formats.md:3:## 1. MLCK Checkpoint Format (`.mlck`)\r\ndocs/formats.md:32:| 40 | 8 | int64 | CreationTimestamp | Unix timestamp (seconds) when checkpoint was created |\r\ndocs/formats.md:95:| 4 | uint32 | Epoch | Training epoch at checkpoint t"]
[1875.67539, "o", "ime |\r\ndocs/formats.md:97:| 8 | float64 | LearningRate | Learning rate at checkpoint time |\r\ndocs/formats.md:99:| ParentHashLen | bytes | ParentHash | ASCII hex SHA-256 of the parent checkpoint file (for lineage) |\r\ndocs/formats.md:150:| `event` | string | Event type: `step`, `epoch_end`, `checkpoint`, `eval` |\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:27:## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:49:### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:60:- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:61:- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:63:- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:65:### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:72:### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:79:### 2.7 Checkpoint In"]
[1875.675469, "o", "tegrity - Signature\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:81:- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:88:- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:89:- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:102:- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:157:Each `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:161:For each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:162:- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:163:- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classifie"]
[1875.675543, "o", "d as an **orphan**.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:14:    \"checkpoints\": [\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:50:    \"checkpoints\": 3,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:59:- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:119:  \"checkpoints\": [\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:127:      \"issues\": []\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:136:      \"issues\": [\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:150:- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:151:- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:152:- `issues`: list of human-readable issue descriptions. Format for tensor checksum mismatch: `\"tensor_checksum_mismatch:<tensor_name>\"`.\r\ndocs/spec.md:5:`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, an"]
[1875.67562, "o", "d produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\ndocs/spec.md:21:| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\ndocs/spec.md:39:- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\ndocs/spec.md:73:- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\ndocs/spec.md:74:- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\ndocs/spec.md:80:Build a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\ndocs/spec.md:83:- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\ndocs/spec.md:115:When a parse error occurs for individual artifacts within a batch operation (e.g., one corrupt checkpoint among several), the tool should continue processing remaining artifacts, report the error in the output, and exit with code 0. Exit code 2 is only for cases where the error prevents any meaningful output.\r\n"]
