[2788.646675, "i", "for f in docs/analysis_rules.md docs/spec.md docs/output_schema.md; do echo \"===== $f\"; nl -ba \"$f\" | sed -n '1,260p'; done\n"]
[2788.647546, "o", "for f in docs/analysis_rules.md docs/spec.md docs/output_schema.md; do echo \"===== $f\"; nl -ba \"$f\" | sed -n '1,260p'; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2788.647718, "o", "===== docs/analysis_rules.md\r\n"]
[2788.651265, "o", "     1\t# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n     6\t\r\n"]
[2788.651361, "o", "     7\tGiven multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n    10\t2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n    11\t   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n    12\t   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **latest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n    13\t3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n    14\t4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n    15"]
[2788.651613, "o", "\t   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n    16\t   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n    19\t\r\n    20\tAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n    21\t- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n    22\t- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n    23\t- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t---\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    34\t- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n    35\t- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n    36\t- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n    37\t- **Req"]
[2788.651754, "o", "uired data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n    38\t- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n    41\t\r\n    42\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    43\t- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n    44\t- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n    45\t- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n    46\t- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n    47\t- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n    52\t- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n    53\t  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n    54\t  - The increase is the first entry "]
[2788.651839, "o", "(no previous to compare)\r\n    55\t- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n    56\t- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n    61\t- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n    62\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    63\t- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n    68\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    69\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    70\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    71\t\r\n    72\t### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n    73\t\r\n    74\t- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-b"]
[2788.651913, "o", "it of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n    75\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    76\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    77\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\t- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n    82\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    83\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    84\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n    85\t\r\n    86\t### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\n    89\t- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n    90\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    91\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n    94\t\r\n    95\t- **Method**: Consecutive timeline en"]
[2788.651969, "o", "tries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n    96\t- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n    97\t- **Severity**: `low`\r\n    98\t- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n    99\t\r\n   100\t### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\t- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n   103\t- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n   104\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n   105\t- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n   106\t\r\n   107\t---\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t## 3. Query Language\r\n   110\t\r\n"]
[2788.652062, "o", "   111\t### 3.1 Grammar\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t```\r\n   114\tquery      := condition (BOOL_OP condition)*\r\n   115\tcondition  := field COMP_OP value\r\n   116\tBOOL_OP    := \"AND\" | \"OR\"\r\n   117\tCOMP_OP    := \">\" | \"<\" | \">=\" | \"<=\" | \"==\" | \"!=\"\r\n   118\tfield      := \"step\" | \"epoch\" | \"loss\" | \"lr\" | \"grad_norm\" | \"acc\" | \"event\" | \"ts\"\r\n   119\tvalue      := NUMBER | QUOTED_STRING | TIMESTAMP\r\n   120\tNUMBER     := integer or float literal\r\n   121\tQUOTED_STRING := '\"' ... '\"' (double-quoted string)\r\n   122\tTIMESTAMP  := ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z)\r\n   123\t```\r\n   124\t\r\n   125\t### 3.2 Operator Precedence\r\n"]
[2788.652126, "o", "   126\t\r\n   127\t- `AND` binds tighter than `OR`\r\n   128\t- Parentheses are NOT supported (keep the grammar simple)\r\n   129\t- Evaluation: left to right with AND having higher precedence\r\n   130\t\r\n   131\tExample: `loss > 1.0 OR grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3`\r\n   132\tParses as: `loss > 1.0 OR (grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3)`\r\n   133\t\r\n   134\t### 3.3 Type Rules\r\n   135"]
[2788.652195, "o", "\t\r\n   136\t- `step`, `epoch`: integer comparisons\r\n   137\t- `loss`, `lr`, `grad_norm`, `acc`: float comparisons (tolerance 1e-9 for `==`)\r\n   138\t- `event`: string comparisons (`==`, `!=` only)\r\n   139\t- `ts`: timestamp comparisons (parse both sides as time, compare chronologically)\r\n   140\t\r\n   141\t### 3.4 Output\r\n   142\t\r\n   143\tJSON array of matching timeline entries (after reconstruction), sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   144\t\r\n"]
[2788.652256, "o", "   145\t### 3.5 Error Handling\r\n   146\t\r\n   147\t- Invalid query syntax: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   148\t- Unknown field name: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   149\t- Type mismatch (e.g., `event > 5`): exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   150\t\r\n   151\t---\r\n   152\t\r\n   153\t## 4. Lineage Graph Construction\r\n"]
[2788.652323, "o", "   154\t\r\n   155\t### 4.1 Node Identification\r\n   156\t\r\n   157\tEach `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t### 4.2 Edge Construction\r\n   160\t\r\n   161\tFor each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:\r\n   162\t- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.\r\n   163\t"]
[2788.652385, "o", "- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classified as an **orphan**.\r\n   164\t\r\n   165\t### 4.3 Graph Validation\r\n   166\t\r\n   167\t- The lineage graph must be a DAG. If a cycle is detected, report each cycle's member nodes.\r\n   168\t- Roots: nodes with no incoming edges and empty `ParentHash`.\r\n   169\t- Leaves: nodes with no outgoing edges.\r\n   170\t\r\n   171\t### 4.4 Topological Sort\r\n   172\t\r\n   173\t"]
[2788.652445, "o", "The lineage output includes a topological ordering of all non-orphan nodes, from root to leaf. If multiple valid orderings exist, sort by `CreationTimestamp` ascending as tiebreaker.\r\n"]
[2788.652859, "o", "===== docs/spec.md\r\n"]
[2788.656179, "o", "     1\t# mlforge - ML Model Artifact Forensics Engine\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## Overview\r\n     4\t\r\n"]
[2788.656262, "o", "     5\t`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## CLI Interface\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\tThe binary is built as `mlforge` and placed at `/app/mlforge` (or on `$PATH` after `go install`).\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t```\r\n    12\tmlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [flags]\r\n    13\t```\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\t### Commands\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t| Command | Description |\r\n    18\t|---------|-------------|\r\n    19\t| `ingest` | Scan evidence directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n    20\t| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n    21\t| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n"]
[2788.656348, "o", "    22\t| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n    23\t| `lineage` | Build and output model lineage DAG |\r\n    24\t"]
[2788.656411, "o", "| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n    25\t| `report` | Generate full forensic report combining all analyses |\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t### Global Flags\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n    30\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n    31\t| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json` or `text` |\r\n    32\t| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n"]
[2788.656498, "o", "    33\t\r\n    34\t### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\t#### `ingest`\r\n    37\t\r\n"]
[2788.656585, "o", "    38\tScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n    39\t- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n    40\t- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n    41\t- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t#### `timeline`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\tParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n    52\t- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n    53\t- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n    54\t- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n"]
[2788.656657, "o", "    55\t\r\n    56\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t#### `verify`\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\tFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n    61\t1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)\r\n    62\t2. Validate the header checksum\r\n    63\t3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n    64\t4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n"]
[2788.656723, "o", "    65\t5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n    66\t\r\n"]
[2788.656822, "o", "    67\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t#### `detect`\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\tRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n    72\t- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n    73\t- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n    74\t- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n    77\t\r\n    78\t#### `lineage`\r\n    79\t\r\n"]
[2788.65692, "o", "    80\tBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\t**Rules**:\r\n    83\t- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n    84\t- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n    85\t- Root nodes have empty `parent_hash`\r\n    86\t- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the evidence set\r\n    87\t- If a cycle is detected, report it as an anomaly (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\".\r\n"]
[2788.656967, "o", "    90\t\r\n    91\t#### `query`\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t```\r\n    94\tmlforge query <evidence-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n    95\t```\r\n    96\t\r\n    97\tFilter the unified timeline using the query expression language defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Query Language\".\r\n    98\t\r\n"]
[2788.657072, "o", "    99\tOutput (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n   100\t\r\n   101\t#### `report`\r\n   102\t\r\n   103\tGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results.\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n   106\t\r\n   107\t## Exit Codes\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t| Code | Meaning |\r\n   110\t|------|---------|\r\n   111\t| 0 | Success |\r\n   112\t| 1 | Input error (missing directory, no artifacts, invalid arguments) |\r\n   113\t| 2 | Parse error (corrupt or unreadable artifact) |\r\n   114\t\r\n"]
[2788.65714, "o", "   115\tWhen a parse error occurs for individual artifacts within a batch operation (e.g., one corrupt checkpoint among several), the tool should continue processing remaining artifacts, report the error in the output, and exit with code 0. Exit code 2 is only for cases where the error prevents any meaningful output.\r\n   116\t\r\n   117\t## Build\r\n   118\t\r\n   119\t```bash\r\n   120\tcd /app && go build -o mlforge ./cmd/mlforge\r\n   121\t```\r\n   122\t\r\n   123\t## Cross-References\r\n   124\t\r\n"]
[2788.65723, "o", "   125\t- Binary formats: `/app/docs/formats.md`\r\n   126\t- Detection algorithms and query language: `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`\r\n   127\t- JSON output schemas: `/app/docs/output_schema.md`\r\n"]
[2788.65761, "o", "===== docs/output_schema.md\r\n"]
[2788.660964, "o", "     1\t# Output Schemas\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tAll commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t---\r\n"]
[2788.661096, "o", "     6\t\r\n     7\t## 1. Ingest Output\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t```json\r\n    10\t{\r\n    11\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    12\t  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\r\n    13\t  \"artifacts\": {\r\n    14\t    \"checkpoints\": [\r\n    15\t      {\r\n    16\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n    17\t        \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n    18\t        \"version\": 1,\r\n    19\t        \"num_tensors\": 12,\r\n    20\t        \"num_metadata\": 3,\r\n    21\t        \"signed\": false,\r\n    22\t        \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    23\t        \"provenance\": {\r\n    24\t          \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    25\t          \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n"]
[2788.66125, "o", "    26\t          \"framework\": \"PyTorch\",\r\n    27\t          \"framework_version\": \"2.1.0\",\r\n    28\t          \"parent_hash\": \"\"\r\n    29\t        }\r\n    30\t      }\r\n    31\t    ],\r\n    32\t    \"log_shards\": [\r\n    33\t      {\r\n    34\t        \"file\": \"shard_001.jsonl\",\r\n    35\t        \"entries\": 500,\r\n    36\t        \"step_range\": [0, 5000],\r\n    37\t        \"epoch_range\": [0, 1],\r\n    38\t        \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\"]\r\n    39\t      }\r\n    40\t    ],\r\n    41\t    \"configs\": [\r\n    42\t      {\r\n    43\t        \"file\": \"config_train.json\",\r\n    44\t        \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n    45\t        \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\"\r\n    46\t      }\r\n    47\t    ]\r\n    48\t  },\r\n"]
[2788.661336, "o", "    49\t  \"totals\": {\r\n    50\t    \"checkpoints\": 3,\r\n    51\t    \"log_shards\": 4,\r\n    52\t    \"configs\": 1\r\n    53\t  }\r\n    54\t}\r\n    55\t```\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t**Field rules:**\r\n    58\t- `file_hash`: SHA-256 hex of the entire `.mlck` file content.\r\n    59\t- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n    60\t- `log_shards` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    61\t- `configs` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    62\t- `step_range`: `[min_step, max_step]` across all entries in the shard.\r\n    63"]
[2788.661407, "o", "\t- `epoch_range`: `[min_epoch, max_epoch]` across all entries.\r\n    64\t- `time_range`: `[earliest_ts, latest_ts]` as ISO 8601 strings.\r\n    65\t\r\n    66\t---\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\t## 2. Timeline Output\r\n    69\t\r\n    70\t```json\r\n    71\t{\r\n    72\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    73\t  \"total_entries\": 1200,\r\n    74\t  \"total_epochs\": 5,\r\n"]
[2788.661466, "o", "    75\t  \"step_range\": [0, 50000],\r\n    76\t  \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-17T14:00:00Z\"],\r\n    77\t  \"conflicts_resolved\": 3,\r\n    78\t  \"gaps\": [\r\n    79\t    {\r\n    80\t      \"after_step\": 5000,"]
[2788.661528, "o", "\r\n    81\t      \"before_step\": 5200,\r\n    82\t      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    83\t      \"gap_steps\": 200,\r\n    84\t      \"after_ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    85\t      \"before_ts\": \"2024-01-15T13:00:00Z\"\r\n    86\t    }\r\n    87\t  ],\r\n    88\t  \"entries\": [\r\n    89\t    {\r\n"]
[2788.661587, "o", "    90\t      \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\",\r\n    91\t      \"epoch\": 0,\r\n    92\t      \"step\": 0,\r\n    93\t      \"loss\": 6.9078,\r\n    94\t      \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n    95\t      \"grad_norm\": 12.34,\r\n    96\t      \"acc\": 0.001,\r\n    97\t      \"event\": \"step\",\r\n    98\t      \"sources\": [\"shard_001.jsonl\"],\r\n"]
[2788.661651, "o", "    99\t      \"conflict\": false\r\n   100\t    }\r\n   101\t  ]\r\n   102\t}\r\n   103\t```\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\t**Field rules:**\r\n   106\t- `entries`: sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   107\t- `sources`: list of shard filenames (basenames) that contained this `(epoch, step)`.\r\n   108\t- `conflict`: `true` if this entry was chosen by conflict resolution.\r\n"]
[2788.661708, "o", "   109\t- `gaps`: only gaps where `gap_steps > 100` within the same epoch.\r\n   110\t- Entries with missing optional fields omit them from the JSON (do not include null).\r\n   111\t\r\n   112\t---\r\n   113\t\r\n   114\t## 3. Verify Output\r\n   115\t\r\n   116\t```json\r\n   117\t{\r\n"]
[2788.661768, "o", "   118\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   119\t  \"checkpoints\": [\r\n   120\t    {\r\n   121\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n   122\t      \"valid\": true,\r\n   123\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n   124\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": true,\r\n   125\t      \"signature_valid\": null,\r\n   126\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   127\t      \"issues\": []\r\n"]
[2788.661833, "o", "   128\t    },\r\n   129\t    {\r\n   130\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   131\t      \"valid\": false,\r\n   132\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n   133\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": false,\r\n   134\t      \"signature_valid\": true,\r\n   135\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   136\t      \"issues\": [\r\n   137\t"]
[2788.661919, "o", "        {\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\"}\r\n   138\t      ]\r\n   139\t    }\r\n   140\t  ],\r\n   141\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   142\t    \"total\": 3,\r\n   143\t    \"valid\": 2,\r\n   144\t    \"invalid\": 1\r\n   145\t  }\r\n   146\t}\r\n   147\t```\r\n   148\t\r\n   149\t**Field rules:**\r\n"]
[2788.661996, "o", "   150\t- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n   151\t- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\n   152\t- `issues`: list of issue objects with `type` (string) and `detail` (string). For example, a tensor checksum mismatch appears as `{\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"<tensor_name>\"}`.\r\n   153\t- `valid`: `true` only if all applicable checks pass.\r\n   154\t\r\n   155\t---\r\n   156\t\r\n   157\t## 4. Detect Output\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t```json\r\n"]
[2788.662057, "o", "   160\t{\r\n   161\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   162\t  \"anomalies\": [\r\n   163\t    {\r\n   164\t      \"id\": \"ANOM-001\",\r\n   165\t      \"type\": \"gradient_spike\",\r\n   166\t      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\n   167\t      \"epoch\": 2,\r\n   168\t      \"step\": 3456,\r\n"]
[2788.662117, "o", "   169\t      \"details\": {\r\n   170\t        \"observed\": 15.3,\r\n   171\t        \"window_mean\": 1.2,\r\n   172\t        \"window_stddev\": 0.3,\r\n   173\t        \"z_score\": 47.0\r\n   174\t      },\r\n   175\t      \"source\": \"shard_002.jsonl\"\r\n   176\t    },\r\n   177\t    {\r\n   178"]
[2788.662178, "o", "\t      \"id\": \"ANOM-002\",\r\n   179\t      \"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\",\r\n   180\t      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\n   181\t      \"details\": {\r\n   182\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   183\t        \"tensor_name\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\",\r\n   184\t        \"expected_checksum\": \"abcd1234...\",\r\n   185\t        \"actual_checksum\": \"efgh5678...\"\r\n   186\t      },\r\n"]
[2788.662242, "o", "   187\t      \"source\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   188\t        \"checkpoint\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\"\r\n   189\t    }\r\n   190\t  ],\r\n   191\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   192\t    \"total\": 5,\r\n   193\t    \"by_severity\": {\r\n   194\t      \"critical\": 1,\r\n   195\t      \"high\": 2,\r\n   196\t      \"medium\": 1,\r\n   197\t      \"low\": 1"]
[2788.662299, "o", "\r\n   198\t    },\r\n   199\t    \"by_type\": {\r\n   200\t      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n   201\t      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n   202\t      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n   203\t      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n   204\t      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n   205\t    }\r\n   206\t  }\r\n"]
[2788.662361, "o", "   207\t}\r\n   208\t```\r\n   209\t\r\n   210\t**Field rules:**\r\n   211\t- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n   212\t- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\r\n   213\t- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n   214\t- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n   215\t- `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.\r\n"]
[2788.662426, "o", "   216\t- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\r\n   217\t- `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\r\n   218\t- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n   219\t\r\n   220\t---\r\n   221\t\r\n   222\t## 5. Lineage Output\r\n   223\t\r\n   224\t```json\r\n   225\t{\r\n"]
[2788.662483, "o", "   226\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   227\t  \"nodes\": [\r\n   228\t    {\r\n   229\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n   230\t      \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n   231\t      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n   232\t      \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n   233\t      \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n   234\t      \"parent_hash\": \"\",\r\n"]
[2788.662541, "o", "   235\t      \"is_root\": true,\r\n   236\t      \"is_leaf\": false,\r\n   237\t      \"is_orphan\": false\r\n   238\t    }\r\n   239\t  ],\r\n   240\t  \"edges\": [\r\n   241\t    {\r\n   242\t      \"from\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n   243\t      \"to\": \"d4e5f6...\",\r\n   244\t      \"from_file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n"]
[2788.662602, "o", "   245\t      \"to_file\": \"model_epoch2.mlck\"\r\n   246\t    }\r\n   247\t  ],\r\n   248\t  \"roots\": [\"a1b2c3...\"],\r\n   249\t  \"leaves\": [\"g7h8i9...\"],\r\n   250\t  \"orphans\": [],\r\n   251\t  \"topological_order\": [\"a1b2c3...\", \"d4e5f6...\", \"g7h8i9...\"],\r\n   252\t  \"cycles\": []\r\n   253\t}\r\n"]
[2788.662659, "o", "   254\t```\r\n   255\t\r\n   256\t**Field rules:**\r\n   257\t- `nodes`: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n   258\t- `edges`: sorted by `from` hash then `to` hash lexicographically.\r\n   259\t- `roots`: file hashes of root nodes (no parent), sorted.\r\n   260\t- `leaves`: file hashes of leaf nodes (no children), sorted.\r\n"]
