[2812.138829, "o", "     1\t# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\tGiven multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n    10\t"]
[2812.139019, "o", "2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n    11\t   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n    12\t   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **latest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n    13\t3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n    14\t4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n    15\t   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n    16\t   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n    19\t\r\n    20\tAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n    21\t- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n    22\t- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n    23\t- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an ad"]
[2812.139154, "o", "ditional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t---\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    34\t- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n    35\t- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n    36\t- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n    37\t- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n    38\t- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n"]
[2812.139774, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2812.139848, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2812.437369, "i", "nl -ba docs/spec.md | sed -n '1,90p'\n"]
[2812.437666, "o", "nl -ba docs/spec.md | sed -n '1,90p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2812.441327, "o", "     1\t# mlforge - ML Model Artifact Forensics Engine\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## Overview\r\n     4\t\r\n"]
[2812.441427, "o", "     5\t`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## CLI Interface\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\tThe binary is built as `mlforge` and placed at `/app/mlforge` (or on `$PATH` after `go install`).\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t```\r\n    12\tmlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [flags]\r\n    13\t```\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\t### Commands\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t| Command | Description |\r\n    18\t|---------|-------------|"]
[2812.441508, "o", "\r\n    19\t| `ingest` | Scan evidence directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n    20\t| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n    21\t| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n    22\t| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n    23\t| `lineage` | Build and output model lineage DAG |\r\n    24\t| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n    25\t| `report` | Generate full forensic report combining all analyses |\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t### Global Flags\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n"]
[2812.441574, "o", "    30\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n    31\t| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json` or `text` |\r\n    32\t| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n    33\t\r\n"]
[2812.441646, "o", "    34\t### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\t#### `ingest`\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\tScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n    39\t- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n    40\t- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n    41\t- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t#### `timeline`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\tParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t"]
[2812.441732, "o", "**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n    52\t- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n    53\t- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n    54\t- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n    55\t"]
[2812.441874, "o", "\r\n    56\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t#### `verify`\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\tFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n    61\t1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)\r\n    62\t2. Validate the header checksum\r\n    63\t3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n    64\t4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n    65\t5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n"]
[2812.441999, "o", "    66\t\r\n    67\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t#### `detect`\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\tRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n    72\t- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n    73\t- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n    74\t- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n    77\t\r\n    78\t#### `lineage`\r\n    79\t\r\n    80\tBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\t**Rules**:\r\n    83\t- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n    84\t- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n    85\t- Root nodes have empty `parent_hash`\r\n    86\t- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the evidence set\r\n"]
[2812.442086, "o", "    87\t- If a cycle is detected, report it as an anomaly (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\".\r\n    90\t\r\n"]
[2812.442489, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2812.442552, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2812.72661, "i", "nl -ba docs/output_schema.md | sed -n '1,130p'\n"]
[2812.726982, "o", "nl -ba docs/output_schema.md | sed -n '1,130p'"]
[2812.727069, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2812.730535, "o", "     1\t# Output Schemas\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tAll commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\r\n     4\t\r\n"]
[2812.730625, "o", "     5\t---\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## 1. Ingest Output\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t```json\r\n    10\t{\r\n    11\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    12\t  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\r\n    13\t  \"artifacts\": {\r\n    14\t    \"checkpoints\": [\r\n    15\t      {\r\n    16\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n    17\t        \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n    18\t        \"version\": 1,\r\n    19"]
[2812.730708, "o", "\t        \"num_tensors\": 12,\r\n    20\t        \"num_metadata\": 3,\r\n    21\t        \"signed\": false,\r\n    22\t        \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    23\t        \"provenance\": {\r\n    24\t          \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    25\t          \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n    26\t          \"framework\": \"PyTorch\",\r\n    27\t          \"framework_version\": \"2.1.0\",\r\n    28\t          \"parent_hash\": \"\"\r\n    29\t        }\r\n    30\t      }\r\n"]
[2812.73077, "o", "    31\t    ],\r\n    32\t    \"log_shards\": [\r\n    33\t      {\r\n    34\t        \"file\": \"shard_001.jsonl\",\r\n    35\t        \"entries\": 500,\r\n    36\t        \"step_range\": [0, 5000],\r\n    37\t        \"epoch_range\": [0, 1],\r\n    38\t        \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\"]\r\n    39\t      }\r\n    40\t    ],\r\n    41\t    \"configs\": [\r\n"]
[2812.730828, "o", "    42\t      {\r\n    43\t        \"file\": \"config_train.json\",\r\n    44\t        \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n    45\t        \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\"\r\n    46\t      }\r\n    47\t    ]\r\n    48\t  },\r\n    49\t  \"totals\": {\r\n    50\t    \"checkpoints\": 3,\r\n    51\t    \"log_shards\": 4,\r\n"]
[2812.730898, "o", "    52\t    \"configs\": 1\r\n    53\t  }\r\n    54\t}\r\n    55\t```\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t**Field rules:**\r\n"]
[2812.731015, "o", "    58\t- `file_hash`: SHA-256 hex of the entire `.mlck` file content.\r\n    59\t- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n    60\t- `log_shards` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    61\t- `configs` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    62\t- `step_range`: `[min_step, max_step]` across all entries in the shard.\r\n    63\t- `epoch_range`: `[min_epoch, max_epoch]` across all entries.\r\n    64\t- `time_range`: `[earliest_ts, latest_ts]` as ISO 8601 strings.\r\n    65\t\r\n    66\t---\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\t## 2. Timeline Output\r\n    69\t\r\n    70\t```json\r\n    71\t{\r\n    72\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    73\t  \"total_entries\": 1200,\r\n    74\t  \"total_epochs\": 5,\r\n    75\t  \"step_range\": [0, 50000],\r\n    76\t  \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-17T14:00:00Z\"],\r\n    77\t  \"conflicts_resolved\": 3,\r\n    78\t  \"gaps\": [\r\n"]
[2812.731105, "o", "    79\t    {\r\n    80\t      \"after_step\": 5000,\r\n    81\t      \"before_step\": 5200,\r\n    82\t      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    83\t      \"gap_steps\": 200,\r\n    84\t      \"after_ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    85\t      \"before_ts\": \"2024-01-15T13:00:00Z\"\r\n    86\t    }\r\n    87\t  ],\r\n    88\t  \"entries\": [\r\n    89\t    {\r\n    90\t      \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\",\r\n    91\t      \"epoch\": 0,\r\n"]
[2812.731171, "o", "    92\t      \"step\": 0,\r\n    93\t      \"loss\": 6.9078,\r\n    94\t      \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n    95\t      \"grad_norm\": 12.34,\r\n    96\t      \"acc\": 0.001,\r\n    97\t      \"event\": \"step\",\r\n    98\t      \"sources\": [\"shard_001.jsonl\"],\r\n    99\t      \"conflict\": false\r\n   100\t    }\r\n   101\t  ]\r\n   102\t}\r\n   103\t```\r\n"]
[2812.731252, "o", "   104\t\r\n   105\t**Field rules:**\r\n   106\t- `entries`: sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   107\t- `sources`: list of shard filenames (basenames) that contained this `(epoch, step)`.\r\n   108\t- `conflict`: `true` if this entry was chosen by conflict resolution.\r\n   109\t- `gaps`: only gaps where `gap_steps > 100` within the same epoch.\r\n   110\t- Entries with missing optional fields omit them from the JSON (do not include null).\r\n   111\t\r\n   112\t---\r\n   113\t\r\n   114\t## 3. Verify Output\r\n   115\t\r\n"]
[2812.731338, "o", "   116\t```json\r\n   117\t{\r\n   118\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   119\t  \"checkpoints\": [\r\n   120\t"]
[2812.731426, "o", "    {\r\n   121\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n   122\t      \"valid\": true,\r\n   123\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n   124\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": true,\r\n   125\t      \"signature_valid\": null,\r\n   126\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   127\t      \"issues\": []\r\n   128\t    },\r\n   129\t    {\r\n   130\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n"]
[2812.731913, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
