[2917.89137, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2918.165058, "i", "sed -n '1,35p' internal/types/types.go\n"]
[2918.16543, "o", "sed -n '1,35p' internal/types/types.go\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2918.168374, "o", "package types\r\n\r\n// TimelineEntry represents one log entry from a JSONL shard.\r\ntype TimelineEntry struct {\r\n\tTs       string   `json:\"ts\"`\r\n\tEpoch    int      `json:\"epoch\"`\r\n\tStep     int      `json:\"step\"`\r\n\tLoss     *float64 `json:\"loss,omitempty\"`\r\n\tLr       *float64 `json:\"lr,omitempty\"`\r\n\tGradNorm *float64 `json:\"grad_norm,omitempty\"`\r\n\tAcc      *float64 `json:\"acc,omitempty\"`\r\n\tEvent    string   `json:\"event,omitempty\"`\r\n\tSources  []string `json:\"sources,omitempty\"`\r\n\tConflict bool     `json:\"conflict\"`\r\n}\r\n"]
[2918.16855, "o", "\r\n// Anomaly represents one detected anomaly in the detect command.\r\ntype Anomaly struct {\r\n\tID         string                 `json:\"id\"`\r\n\tType       string                 `json:\"type\"`\r\n\tSeverity   string                 `json:\"severity\"`\r\n\tEpoch      *int                   `json:\"epoch,omitempty\"`\r\n\tStep       *int                   `json:\"step,omitempty\"`\r\n\tDetails    map[string]interface{} `json:\"details,omitempty\"`\r\n\tSource     string                 `json:\"source,omitempty\"`\r\n\tCheckpoint string                 `json:\"checkpoint,omitempty\"`\r\n}\r\n\r\n// TensorInfo holds metadata for one tensor in a checkpoint.\r\ntype TensorInfo struct {\r\n\tName  string   `json:\"name\"`\r\n\tDtype byte     `json:\"dtype\"`\r\n\tShape []uint32 `json:\"shape\"`\r\n\tData  []byte   `json:\"-\"`\r\n\tHash  [32]byte `json:\"-\"` // Stored SHA-256\r\n"]
[2918.168994, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2918.16907, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2918.458258, "i", "sed -n '1,30p' docs/analysis_rules.md\n"]
[2918.458571, "o", "sed -n '1,30p' docs/analysis_rules.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2918.461443, "o", "# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n\r\n## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n\r\nGiven multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n\r\n1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n"]
[2918.461572, "o", "2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **latest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n\r\nAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n\r\nAnomalies are "]
[2918.461664, "o", "classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n\r\n"]
[2918.462071, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2918.462145, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2918.709731, "i", "sed -n '45,60p' docs/spec.md\n"]
[2918.710068, "o", "sed -n '45,60p' docs/spec.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2918.713363, "o", "If the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n\r\n#### `timeline`\r\n\r\nParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n\r\n**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n\r\n"]
[2918.713424, "o", "Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `verify`\r\n\r\nFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n"]
[2918.713994, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[2935.010063, "i", "grep -R \"Dtype\\|float32\\|dtype\" -n internal/types internal/checkpoint internal/forensics | head -60\n"]
[2935.01075, "o", "grep -R \"Dtype\\|float32\\|dtype\" -n internal/types internal/checkpoint internal/forensics | head -60\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
