[3221.453306, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3221.456154, "o", "# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n\r\n## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n\r\n"]
[3221.456232, "o", "Given multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n\r\n1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy."]
[3221.45629, "o", "\r\n   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **earliest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n\r\nAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n"]
[3221.456706, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[3221.456773, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[3221.45692, "o", "sed -n '95,120p' docs/spec.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3221.459781, "o", "```\r\n\r\nFilter the unified timeline using the query expression language defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Query Language\".\r\n\r\n"]
[3221.459795, "o", "Output (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n\r\n#### `diff`\r\n\r\n"]
[3221.45988, "o", "```\r\nmlforge diff <evidence-dir> <file1> <file2>\r\n```\r\n\r\nCompare two checkpoint files inside `<evidence-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<evidence-dir>`.\r\n\r\nFor every tensor name present in either file, include one entry in `tensor_diffs`, sorted by tensor name lexicographically. `max_abs_diff` and `mean_abs_diff` are included only when both files contain the tensor and their shapes match.\r\n\r\nIf either checkpoint filename does not exist under `<evidence-dir>`, exit non-zero and print an error to stderr.\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Diff Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `report`\r\n\r\nGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results.\r\n\r\n"]
[3221.459902, "o", "Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n\r\n"]
[3221.460374, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[3221.460406, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[3221.460649, "o", "sed -n '318,375p' docs/output_schema.md\r\n"]
[3221.460668, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3221.463502, "o", "\r\n\r\n## 8. Diff Output\r\n"]
[3221.463515, "o", "\r\n```json\r\n"]
[3221.46353, "o", "{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"file_a\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\","]
[3221.463564, "o", "\r\n"]
[3221.463573, "o", "  \"file_b\": \"model_epoch2.mlck\",\r\n  \"tensor_diffs\": [\r\n"]
[3221.463594, "o", "    {\r\n      \"name\": \"layer1.weight\",\r\n      \"shape_match\": true,\r\n"]
[3221.463611, "o", "      \"shape_a\": [4, 3],\r\n"]
[3221.463619, "o", "      \"shape_b\": [4, 3],\r\n"]
[3221.463637, "o", "      \"max_abs_diff\": 1.234,\r\n      \"mean_abs_diff\": 0.567\r\n    },\r\n"]
[3221.463646, "o", "    {\r\n"]
[3221.463654, "o", "      \"name\": \"layer2.weight\",\r\n"]
[3221.463665, "o", "      \"shape_match\": false,\r\n"]
[3221.463697, "o", "      \"shape_a\": [4, 3],\r\n      \"shape_b\": [8, 3]\r\n"]
[3221.463706, "o", "    },\r\n    {\r\n"]
[3221.463713, "o", "      \"name\": \"layer3.bias\",\r\n"]
[3221.46372, "o", "      \"shape_match\": false,\r\n      \"shape_a\": null,\r\n      \"shape_b\": [3]\r\n"]
[3221.50165, "o", "    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"total_tensors_a\": 2,\r\n    \"total_tensors_b\": 2,\r\n    \"common_tensors\": 2,\r\n    \"shape_mismatches\": 0,\r\n    \"only_in_a\": [],\r\n    \"only_in_b\": []\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `file_a` and `file_b` are the basenames of `file1` and `file2`.\r\n- `tensor_diffs`: sorted by tensor name lexicographically.\r\n- `shape_a` and `shape_b`: tensor shapes from each file, or `null` if absent from that file.\r\n- `shape_match`: `true` only when the tensor exists in both files and the shapes are identical.\r\n- `max_abs_diff` and `mean_abs_diff`: present only for tensors with `shape_match: true`, computed over float32 element-wise absolute differences.\r\n- `summary.total_tensors_a` and `summary.total_tensors_b`: tensor counts in each file.\r\n- `summary.common_tensors`: number of tensor names present in both files.\r\n- `summary.shape_mismatches`: number of common tensors with different shapes.\r\n- `summary.only_in_a` and `summary.only_in_b`: tensor names present in only one file, sorted lexicograph"]
[3221.501756, "o", "ically.\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[3229.233683, "i", "go vet ./...\n"]
[3229.23399, "o", "go vet ./...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
