[4549.35505, "o", "cat -n docs/spec.md | sed -n '1,90p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4549.358649, "o", "     1\t# mlforge - ML Model Artifact Forensics Engine\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## Overview\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## CLI Interface\r\n"]
[4549.358767, "o", "     8\t\r\n     9\tThe binary is built as `mlforge` and placed at `/app/mlforge` (or on `$PATH` after `go install`).\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t```\r\n    12\tmlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [flags]\r\n    13\t```\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\t### Commands\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t| Command | Description |\r\n    18\t|---------|-------------|\r\n    19\t| `ingest` | Scan evidence directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n    20\t| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n    21\t| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n    22\t| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n    23\t| `lineage` | Build and output model lineage DAG |\r\n    24\t| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n    25\t| `report` | Generate full forensic report combining all analyses |\r\n    26\t\r\n"]
[4549.35884, "o", "    27\t### Global Flags\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n    30\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n    31\t| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json` or `text` |\r\n    32\t| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n    33\t\r\n    34\t### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\t#### `ingest`\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\tScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n    39\t"]
[4549.358902, "o", "- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n    40\t- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n    41\t- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t#### `timeline`\r\n    48\t\r\n"]
[4549.358975, "o", "    49\tParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n    52\t- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n    53\t- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n    54\t- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n    57\t\r\n"]
[4549.359043, "o", "    58\t#### `verify`\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\tFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n    61\t1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)\r\n    62\t2. Validate the header checksum\r\n    63\t3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n    64\t4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n    65\t5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n"]
[4549.359103, "o", "    68\t\r\n    69\t#### `detect`\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\tRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n    72\t- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n    73\t- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n    74\t- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n    77"]
[4549.359163, "o", "\t\r\n    78\t#### `lineage`\r\n    79\t\r\n    80\tBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\t**Rules**:\r\n    83\t- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n    84\t- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n    85\t- Root nodes have empty `parent_hash`\r\n    86\t"]
[4549.359221, "o", "- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the evidence set\r\n    87\t- If a cycle is detected, report it as an anomaly (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\".\r\n    90\t\r\n"]
[4549.359809, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4549.359873, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[4549.624991, "i", "cat -n docs/spec.md | sed -n '91,160p'\n"]
[4549.625188, "o", "cat -n docs/spec.md | sed -n '91,160p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4549.628327, "o", "    91\t#### `query`\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t```\r\n    94\tmlforge query <evidence-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n    95\t```\r\n"]
[4549.628385, "o", "    96\t\r\n    97\tFilter the unified timeline using the query expression language defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Query Language\".\r\n    98\t\r\n    99\tOutput (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n   100\t\r\n   101\t#### `diff`\r\n   102\t\r\n   103\t```\r\n   104\tmlforge diff <evidence-dir> <file1> <file2>\r\n   105\t```\r\n"]
[4549.628434, "o", "   106\t\r\n   107\tCompare two checkpoint files inside `<evidence-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<evidence-dir>`.\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\tFor every tensor name present in either file, include one entry in `tensor_diffs`, sorted by tensor name lexicographically. `max_abs_diff` and `mean_abs_diff` are included only when both files contain the tensor and their shapes match.\r\n   110\t\r\n   111\tIf either checkpoint filename does not exist under `<evidence-dir>`, exit non-zero and print an error to stderr.\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Diff Output\".\r\n"]
[4549.62848, "o", "   114\t\r\n   115\t#### `report`\r\n   116\t\r\n   117\tGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results.\r\n   118\t\r\n   119\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n   120\t\r\n   121\t## Exit Codes\r\n   122\t\r\n"]
[4549.628525, "o", "   123\t| Code | Meaning |\r\n   124\t|------|---------|\r\n   125\t| 0 | Success |\r\n   126\t| 1 | Input error (missing directory, no artifacts, invalid arguments) |\r\n   127\t| 2 | Parse error (corrupt or unreadable artifact) |\r\n   128\t\r\n   129\tWhen a parse error occurs for individual artifacts within a batch operation (e.g., one corrupt checkpoint among several), the tool should continue processing remaining artifacts, report the error in the output, and exit with code 0. Exit code 2 is only for cases where the error prevents any meaningful output."]
[4549.628566, "o", "\r\n   130\t\r\n   131\t## Build\r\n   132\t\r\n   133\t```bash\r\n   134\tcd /app && go build -o mlforge ./cmd/mlforge\r\n   135\t```\r\n   136\t\r\n"]
[4549.62861, "o", "   137\t## Cross-References\r\n   138\t\r\n   139\t- Binary formats: `/app/docs/formats.md`\r\n   140\t- Detection algorithms and query language: `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`\r\n   141\t- JSON output schemas: `/app/docs/output_schema.md`\r\n"]
[4549.629033, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[4556.364892, "i", "cat -n cmd/mlforge/main.go | sed -n '1,80p'\n"]
[4556.365178, "o", "cat -n cmd/mlforge/main.go | sed -n '1,80p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4556.368699, "o", "     1\tpackage main\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\timport (\r\n     4\t\t\"encoding/json\"\r\n     5\t\t\"fmt\"\r\n"]
[4556.36881, "o", "     6\t\t\"os\"\r\n     7\t\t\"strings\"\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t\t\"mlforge/internal/forensics\"\r\n    10\t)\r\n    11\t\r\n    12\tfunc main() {\r\n    13\t\t// --- Parse flags ---------------------------------------------------\r\n    14\t\tformat := \"json\"\r\n    15\t\tverbose := false\r\n    16\t\tvar positional []string\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t\tfor _, arg := range os.Args[1:] {\r\n    19\t\t\tswitch {\r\n    20\t\t\tcase arg == \"--verbose\":\r\n    21\t\t\t\tverbose = true\r\n"]
[4556.36889, "o", "    22\t\t\tcase strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--format=\"):\r\n    23\t\t\t\tformat = strings.TrimPrefix(arg, \"--format=\")\r\n    24\t\t\tcase arg == \"--format\":\r\n    25\t\t\t// handled below as two-token flag\r\n"]
[4556.368971, "o", "    26\t\t\tdefault:\r\n    27\t\t\t\tpositional = append(positional, arg)\r\n    28\t\t\t}\r\n    29\t\t}\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t\t// Handle \"--format json\" (two separate tokens)\r\n    32\t\tfor i := 1; i < len(os.Args)-1; i++ {\r\n    33\t\t\tif os.Args[i] == \"--format\" {\r\n    34\t\t\t\tformat = os.Args[i+1]\r\n    35\t\t\t\t// Remove the value from positional args\r\n    36\t\t\t\tfiltered := positional[:0]\r\n    37\t\t\t\tfor _, p := range positional {\r\n    38\t\t\t\t\tif p != os.Args[i+1] {\r\n    39\t\t\t\t\t\tfiltered = append(filtered, p)\r\n    40\t\t\t\t\t}\r\n    41"]
[4556.369038, "o", "\t\t\t\t}\r\n    42\t\t\t\tpositional = filtered\r\n    43\t\t\t\tbreak\r\n    44\t\t\t}\r\n    45\t\t}\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t\tif format != \"json\" && format != \"text\" {\r\n    48\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"invalid format %q: must be json or text\\n\", format)\r\n"]
[4556.369103, "o", "    49\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\n    50\t\t}\r\n    51\t\r\n    52\t\t_ = verbose // reserved for diagnostic output\r\n    53\t\r\n    54\t\t// --- Validate positional args --------------------------------------\r\n    55\t\tif len(positional) < 2 {\r\n    56\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Usage: mlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [args...]\\n\")\r\n    57\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\r\n"]
[4556.369164, "o", "    58\t\t}\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t\tcmd := positional[0]\r\n    61\t\tdir := positional[1]\r\n    62\t\r\n    63\t\t// --- Route to command handler --------------------------------------\r\n    64\t\tvar result interface{}\r\n    65\t\tvar err error\r\n    66\t\r\n    67"]
[4556.369227, "o", "\t\tswitch cmd {\r\n    68\t\tcase \"ingest\":\r\n    69\t\t\tresult, err = forensics.BuildIngest(dir)\r\n    70\t\tcase \"timeline\":\r\n    71\t\t\tresult, err = forensics.BuildTimeline(dir)\r\n    72\t\tcase \"verify\":\r\n    73\t\t\tresult, err = forensics.BuildVerify(dir)\r\n    74\t\tcase \"detect\":\r\n    75\t\t\t"]
[4556.36929, "o", "result, err = forensics.BuildDetect(dir)\r\n    76\t\tcase \"lineage\":\r\n    77\t\t\tresult, err = forensics.BuildLineage(dir)\r\n    78\t\tcase \"query\":\r\n    79\t\t\tif len(positional) < 3 {\r\n    80\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Usage: mlforge query <dir> \\\"<expression>\\\"\\n\")\r\n"]
[4556.36972, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[4563.525557, "i", "grep -nE 'detect|Detect|evidence|Evidence|format|csv|severity|filter|anomaly|Anomaly' docs/spec.md\n"]
[4563.526705, "o", "grep -nE 'detect|Detect|evidence|Evidence|format|csv|severity|filter|anomaly|Anomaly' docs/spec.md\r\n"]
[4563.526811, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4563.530766, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Ks anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-backed forensic reports.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K12\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlforge <command> <\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir> [flags]\r\n"]
[4563.530879, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K19\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `ingest` | Scan \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n"]
[4563.530956, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K22\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[K` | Run \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Kion across all \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K |\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K24\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `query` | Query the unified timeline with \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter\u001b[m\u001b[K expressions |\r\n"]
[4563.531018, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K31\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[K` | string | `json` | Output \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[K: `json` or `text` |\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K38\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KScan `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>` recursively for:\r\n"]
[4563.531081, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K45\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KIf the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K49\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n"]
[4563.531151, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K54\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Gaps in the step sequence are \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Ked and reported\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K60\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KFor each `.mlck` file in `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`:\r\n"]
[4563.531213, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K61\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K1. Parse the file according to the MLCK \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[K (see `/app/docs/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[Ks.md`)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K69\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K#### `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[K`\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K71\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KRun all \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Kion rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K:\r\n"]
[4563.531284, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K76\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KDetect\u001b[m\u001b[K Output\".\r\n"]
[4563.531347, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K86\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K set\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K87\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- If a cycle is \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Ked, report it as an \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K94\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlforge query <\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K104\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlforge diff <\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir> <file1> <file2>\r\n"]
[4563.531414, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K107\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KCompare two checkpoint files inside `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K111\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KIf either checkpoint filename does not exist under `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`, exit non-zero and print an error to stderr.\r\n"]
[4563.531475, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K117\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[K, lineage) and combining results.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K139\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Binary \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[Ks: `/app/docs/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[Ks.md`\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K140\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KDetect\u001b[m\u001b[Kion algorithms and query language: `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`\r\n"]
