[4563.824505, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K12\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K_dir\": \"/path/to/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K\",\r\n"]
[4563.824731, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K157\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K## 4. \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KDetect\u001b[m\u001b[K Output\r\n"]
[4563.824856, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K166\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseverity\u001b[m\u001b[K\": \"high\",\r\n"]
[4563.824925, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K180\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseverity\u001b[m\u001b[K\": \"critical\",\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K193\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K    \"by_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseverity\u001b[m\u001b[K\": {\r\n"]
[4563.825032, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K204\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"lr_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K\": 1\r\n"]
[4563.825119, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K211\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `id`: Sequential ID in \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kformat\u001b[m\u001b[K `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Kion order.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K212\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `anomalies`: sorted by \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kseverity\u001b[m\u001b[K (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K213\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n"]
[4563.8252, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K215\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `source`: the artifact file where the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K was \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Ked.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K217\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `checkpoint`: present when the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kanomaly\u001b[m\u001b[K is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K218\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- If no anomalies are \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[Ked, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n"]
[4563.825265, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K273\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K_dir\": \"/path/to/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K\",\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K277\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[K\": { ... },\r\n"]
[4563.825319, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K285\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Each section (`ingest`, `timeline`, `verify`, `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdetect\u001b[m\u001b[K`, `lineage`) contains the exact same JSON structure as the corresponding standalone command output.\r\n"]
[4563.825857, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4563.825921, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[4570.194449, "i", "cat -n docs/spec.md | sed -n '20,80p'\n"]
[4570.194767, "o", "cat -n docs/spec.md | sed -n '20,80p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[4570.198411, "o", "    20\t| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n    21\t| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n    22\t| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n    23\t| `lineage` | Build and output model lineage DAG |\r\n    24\t| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n    25\t| `report` | Generate full forensic report combining all analyses |\r\n"]
[4570.198547, "o", "    26\t\r\n    27\t### Global Flags\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n    30\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n    31\t| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json` or `text` |\r\n    32\t| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n    33\t\r\n    34\t### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\t#### `ingest`\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\tScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n    39\t- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n    40\t- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n    41\t- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t#### `timeline`\r\n    48\t\r\n"]
[4570.198628, "o", "    49\tParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n    52\t- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n    53\t- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n    54\t- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t#### `verify`\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\tFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n    61\t1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)"]
[4570.198721, "o", "\r\n    62\t2. Validate the header checksum\r\n    63\t3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n    64\t4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n    65\t5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t#### `detect`\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\tRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n    72\t- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n    73\t- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n"]
[4570.198802, "o", "    74\t- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n    77\t\r\n    78\t#### `lineage`\r\n"]
[4570.198865, "o", "    79\t\r\n    80\tBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n"]
[4570.199302, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[4570.199362, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
