[5185.61127, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>     }\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.611335, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ],\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.611399, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.61144, "o", "  \"summary\": {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.611513, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.611585, "o", "    \"total\": 5,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.611684, "o", "    \"by_severity\": {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.611749, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.611818, "o", "      \"critical\": 1,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.611883, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.611957, "o", "      \"high\": 2,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.61205, "o", "      \"medium\": 1,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.612107, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.61218, "o", "      \"low\": 1\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[5185.612237, "o", ">     },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.612292, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.612354, "o", "    \"by_type\": {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.61242, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.612507, "o", "      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.612573, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.612663, "o", "      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.612728, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.612858, "o", "      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.612925, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.613028, "o", "      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613093, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.613172, "o", "      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613235, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>     }\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613291, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   }\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613347, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> }\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613419, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.613478, "o", "```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.613532, "o", "**Field rules:**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613593, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.613763, "o", "- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.613824, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.614049, "o", "- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.614105, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.614745, "o", "- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.614803, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.615024, "o", "- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.616587, "o", "- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.616797, "o", "- `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.617014, "o", "- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.617483, "o", "- `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.617744, "o", "- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.6178, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.617963, "o", "- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[5185.618036, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.618129, "o", "### Detect CSV Output\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.618467, "o", "When `--format csv` is used with `detect`, the command outputs CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.618552, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ```text\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[5185.618698, "o", "id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.618762, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5185.618818, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
