[5196.59901, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K12\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K_dir\": \"/path/to/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K\",\r\n"]
[5196.599129, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K175\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K\": {\r\n"]
[5196.599216, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K176\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K        \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kwindow_values\u001b[m\u001b[K\": [1.1, 1.3, 1.0, 1.2, 1.4]\r\n"]
[5196.599232, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K190\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K\": {},\r\n"]
[5196.599308, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K219\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kwindow_values\u001b[m\u001b[K`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K object: `{}`.\r\n"]
[5196.59943, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K223\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K` is supplied.\r\n"]
[5196.599491, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K226\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K### Detect \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KCSV\u001b[m\u001b[K Output\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K228\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KWhen `--format \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcsv\u001b[m\u001b[K` is used with `detect`, the command outputs \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KCSV\u001b[m\u001b[K instead of JSON. The \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KCSV\u001b[m\u001b[K header is exactly:\r\n"]
[5196.599552, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K234\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KOne header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K LEVEL` applies before \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KCSV\u001b[m\u001b[K output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K289\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K  \"\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K_dir\": \"/path/to/\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K\",\r\n"]
[5196.599668, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K5\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-backed forensic reports.\r\n"]
[5196.59972, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K12\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlforge <command> <\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir> [flags]\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K19\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `ingest` | Scan \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n"]
[5196.599772, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K22\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K |\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K31\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json`, `text`, or `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcsv\u001b[m\u001b[K` (`\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcsv\u001b[m\u001b[K` is supported only by `detect`) |\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K38\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KScan `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>` recursively for:\r\n"]
[5196.599822, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K45\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KIf the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K49\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KParse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K60\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KFor each `.mlck` file in `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`:\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K71\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K:\r\n"]
[5196.59988, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K76\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KEvery anomaly object includes a top-level `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K` field. Timeline-based anomalies include `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kwindow_values\u001b[m\u001b[K` with up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies have an empty `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K` object.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K79\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--format \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcsv\u001b[m\u001b[K`: output \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KCSV\u001b[m\u001b[K instead of JSON. The \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KCSV\u001b[m\u001b[K header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.\r\n"]
[5196.599939, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K80\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the specified severity level or above. Severity order is `critical > high > medium > low`. For example, `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K high` shows only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K critical` shows only `critical` anomalies. The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.\r\n"]
[5196.599983, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K92\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K set\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K100\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlforge query <\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K110\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[Kmlforge diff <\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir> <file1> <file2>\r\n"]
[5196.600038, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K113\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KCompare two checkpoint files inside `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`.\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K117\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KIf either checkpoint filename does not exist under `<\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kevidence\u001b[m\u001b[K-dir>`, exit non-zero and print an error to stderr.\r\n"]
