[5424.494859, "o", "docs/formats.md:43:| 1 | uint8 | Dtype | Data type enum (see below) |\r\ndocs/formats.md:82:Located at `ProvenanceOffset`. Fixed structure followed by variable-length fields:\r\ndocs/formats.md:164:Training configuration files follow the naming pattern `config_*.json`:\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:7:Given multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:29:Anomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:36:- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:45:- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:55:- **Severity**: `medium`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:62:- **Severity**: `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:69:- **Severity**: `critical`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:76:- **Severity**: `critical`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:83:- **Severity**: `critical`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:90:- **Severity**: `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:97:- **Severity**: `low`\r\ndocs/analysis"]
[5424.495023, "o", "_rules.md:104:- **Severity**: `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:130:- `NOT` is a prefix operator with the highest precedence.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:166:      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:183:      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:197:    \"by_severity\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:198:      \"critical\": 1,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:199:      \"high\": 2,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:200:      \"medium\": 1,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:201:      \"low\": 1\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:216:- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:219:- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful precedin"]
[5424.495096, "o", "g window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:223:- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:231:id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:234:One header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\ndocs/spec.md:79:- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.\r\ndocs/spec.md:80:- `--filter-severity LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the"]
[5424.495162, "o", " specified severity level or above. Severity order is `critical > high > medium > low`. For example, `--filter-severity high` shows only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--filter-severity critical` shows only `critical` anomalies. The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.\r\ninternal/types/types.go:21:\tSeverity   string                 `json:\"severity\"`\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:26:// ShardInfo holds summary info about one parsed shard.\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:76:\tinfo := ShardInfo{\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:111:\t\tinfo.Entries++\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:112:\t\tif raw.Step < info.MinStep {\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:113:\t\t\tinfo.MinStep = raw.Step\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:115:\t\tif raw.Step > info.MaxStep {\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:116:\t\t\tinfo.MaxStep = raw.Step\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:118:\t\tif raw.Epoch < info.MinEpoch {\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:119:\t\t\tinfo.MinEpoch = raw.Epoch\r\ninternal/logparser/logparser.go:121:\t\tif"]
[5424.495219, "o", " raw.Epoch > info.MaxEpoch {\r\ninternal/lo"]
