[5453.226178, "o", "     1\t# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t"]
[5453.2264, "o", "Given multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n    10\t2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n    11\t   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n    12\t   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **earliest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n    13\t3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n    14\t4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n    15\t   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n    16\t   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n    19\t\r\n    20\tAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n    21\t- All original"]
[5453.226546, "o", " fields from the winning entry\r\n    22\t- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n    23\t- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t---\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    34\t- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n    35\t- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n    36\t- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n    37\t- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n    38\t- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n    41\t\r\n    42\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    43\t- **Method**: Compare loss at window"]
[5453.226654, "o", " start vs window end\r\n    44\t- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n    45\t- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n    46\t- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n    47\t- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n    52\t- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n    53\t  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n    54\t  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n    55\t- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n    56\t- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/ste"]
[5453.226754, "o", "p)\r\n    61\t- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n    62\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    63\t- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n    68\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    69\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    70\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    71\t\r\n    72\t### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n    73\t\r\n    74\t- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n    75\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    76\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    77\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\t- **Meth"]
[5453.226848, "o", "od**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n    82\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    83\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    84\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n    85\t\r\n    86\t### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\n    89\t- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n    90\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    91\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n    94\t\r\n    95\t- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n    96\t- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n    97\t- **Severity**: `low`\r\n    98\t- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n    99\t\r"]
[5453.22695, "o", "\n   100\t### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\t- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n   103\t- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n   104\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n   105\t- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n   106\t\r\n   107\t---\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t## 3. Query Language\r\n   110\t\r\n   111\t### 3.1 Grammar\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t```\r\n   114\tquery      := or_expr\r\n   115\tor_expr    := and_expr (\"OR\" and_expr)*\r\n   116\tand_expr   := not_expr (\"AND\" not_expr)*\r\n   117\tnot_expr   := \"NOT\" not_expr | atom\r\n   118\tatom       := \"(\" or_expr \")\" | condition\r\n   119\tcondition  := field COMP_OP value\r\n   120\tCOMP_OP    := \">\" | \"<\" | \">=\" | \"<=\" | \"==\" | \"!=\"\r\n"]
[5453.227044, "o", "   121\tfield      := \"step\" | \"epoch\" | \"loss\" | \"lr\" | \"grad_norm\" | \"acc\" | \"event\" | \"ts\"\r\n   122\tvalue      := NUMBER | QUOTED_STRING | TIMESTAMP\r\n   123\tNUMBER     := integer or float literal\r\n   124\tQUOTED_STRING := '\"' ... '\"' (double-quoted string)\r\n   125\tTIMESTAMP  := ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z)\r\n   126\t```\r\n   127\t\r\n   128\t### 3.2 Operator Precedence\r\n   129\t\r\n   130\t- `NOT` is a prefix operator with the highest precedence.\r\n   131\t- `AND` binds tighter than `OR`.\r\n   132\t- Parentheses `(` `)` override the default precedence.\r\n   133\t- Malformed parenthesized queries, such as `(step < 5` or `step < 5)`, are invalid query syntax.\r\n   134\t\r\n"]
[5453.227142, "o", "   135\tExamples:\r\n   136\t\r\n   137\t- `NOT epoch == 0` parses as `NOT (epoch == 0)`.\r\n   138\t- `loss > 1.0 OR grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3` parses as `loss > 1.0 OR (grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3)`.\r\n   139\t- `loss > 1.0 OR NOT grad_norm > 5.0 AND epoch == 3` parses as `loss > 1.0 OR ((NOT (grad_norm > 5.0)) AND epoch == 3)`.\r\n   140\t- `(step < 5 OR step > 95) AND epoch == 0` first groups the `OR`, then applies the `AND`.\r\n   141\t\r\n   142\t### 3.3 Type Rules\r\n   143\t\r\n   144\t- `step`, `epoch`: integer comparisons\r\n   145\t- `loss`, `lr`, `grad_norm`, `acc`: float comparisons (tolerance 1e-9 for `==`)\r\n   146\t- `event`: string comparisons (`==`, `!=` only)\r\n   147\t- `ts`: timestamp comparisons (parse both sides as time, compare chronologically)\r\n   148\t\r\n   149"]
[5453.227231, "o", "\t### 3.4 Output\r\n   150\t\r\n   151\tJSON array of matching timeline entries (after reconstruction), sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   152\t\r\n   153\t### 3.5 Error Handling\r\n   154\t\r\n   155\t- Invalid query syntax: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   156\t- Unknown field name: exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   157\t- Type mismatch (e.g., `event > 5`): exit code 1, error message to stderr\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t---\r\n   160\t\r\n   161\t## 4. Lineage Graph Construction\r\n   162\t\r\n   163\t### 4.1 Node Identification\r\n"]
[5453.227319, "o", "   164\t\r\n   165\tEach `.mlck` checkpoint file is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its entire file content (hex-encoded).\r\n   166\t\r\n   167\t### 4.2 Edge Construction\r\n   168\t\r\n   169\tFor each checkpoint with a non-empty `ParentHash` in the provenance section:\r\n   170\t- If a checkpoint with that SHA-256 file hash exists in the evidence set, create a directed edge from parent to child.\r\n   171\t- If no matching parent is found, the checkpoint is classified as an **orphan**.\r\n   172\t\r\n   173\t### 4.3 Graph Validation\r\n   174\t\r\n   175\t- The lineage graph must be a DAG. If a cycle is detected, report each cycle's member nodes.\r\n"]
[5453.227403, "o", "   176\t- Roots: nodes with no incoming edges and empty `ParentHash`.\r\n   177\t- Leaves: nodes with no outgoing edges.\r\n   178\t\r\n   179\t### 4.4 Topological Sort\r\n   180\t\r\n"]
[5453.227747, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[5453.507312, "i", "nl -ba docs/output_schema.md | sed -n '1,260p'\n"]
[5453.507696, "o", "nl -ba docs/output_schema.md | sed -n '1,260p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5453.511347, "o", "     1\t# Output Schemas\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tAll commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t---\r\n     6\t\r\n"]
[5453.511469, "o", "     7\t## 1. Ingest Output\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t```json\r\n    10\t{\r\n    11\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    12\t  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\r\n    13\t  \"artifacts\": {\r\n    14\t    \"checkpoints\": [\r\n    15\t      {\r\n    16\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n    17\t        \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n    18\t        \"version\": 1,\r\n    19\t        \"num_tensors\": 12,\r\n    20\t        \"num_metadata\": 3,\r\n    21\t        \"signed\": false,\r\n    22\t        \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    23\t        \"provenance\": {\r\n    24\t          \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    25\t          \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n    26\t          \"framework\": \"PyTorch\",\r\n    27\t          \"framework_version\": \"2.1.0\",\r\n"]
[5453.511568, "o", "    28\t          \"parent_hash\": \"\"\r\n    29\t        }\r\n    30\t      }\r\n    31\t    ],\r\n    32\t    \"log_shards\": [\r\n    33\t      {\r\n    34\t        \"file\": \"shard_001.jsonl\",\r\n    35\t        \"entries\": 500,\r\n    36\t        \"step_range\": [0, 5000],\r\n    37\t        \"epoch_range\": [0, 1],\r\n    38\t        \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\"]\r\n    39\t      }\r\n    40\t    ],\r\n    41\t    \"configs\": [\r\n    42\t      {\r\n    43\t        \"file\": \"config_train.json\",\r\n"]
[5453.511713, "o", "    44\t        \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n    45\t        \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\"\r\n    46\t      }\r\n    47\t    ]\r\n    48\t  },\r\n    49\t  \"totals\": {\r\n    50\t    \"checkpoints\": 3,\r\n    51\t    \"log_shards\": 4,\r\n    52\t    \"configs\": 1\r\n    53\t  }\r\n    54\t}\r\n    55\t```\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t**Field rules:**\r\n    58\t- `file_hash`: SHA-256 hex of the entire `.mlck` file content.\r\n    59\t- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n    60\t- `log_shards` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    61\t- `configs` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    62\t- `step_range`: `[min_step, max_step]` across all entries in the shard.\r\n    63\t- `epoch_range`: `[min_epoch, max_epoch]` across all entries.\r\n"]
[5453.511821, "o", "    64\t- `time_range`: `[earliest_ts, latest_ts]` as ISO 8601 strings.\r\n    65\t\r\n    66\t---\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\t## 2. Timeline Output\r\n    69\t\r\n    70\t```json\r\n    71\t{\r\n    72\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    73\t  \"total_entries\": 1200,\r\n    74\t  \"total_epochs\": 5,\r\n    75\t  \"step_range\": [0, 50000],\r\n    76\t  \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-17T14:00:00Z\"],\r\n    77\t  \"conflicts_resolved\": 3,\r\n    78\t  \"gaps\": [\r\n    79\t    {\r\n    80\t      \"after_step\": 5000,\r\n    81\t      \"before_step\": 5200,\r\n"]
[5453.511905, "o", "    82\t      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    83\t      \"gap_steps\": 200,\r\n    84\t      \"after_ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    85\t      \"before_ts\": \"2024-01-15T13:00:00Z\"\r\n    86\t    }\r\n    87\t  ],\r\n"]
[5453.512008, "o", "    88\t  \"entries\": [\r\n    89\t    {\r\n    90\t      \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\",\r\n    91\t      \"epoch\": 0,\r\n    92\t      \"step\": 0,\r\n    93\t      \"loss\": 6.9078,\r\n    94\t      \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n    95\t      \"grad_norm\": 12.34,\r\n    96\t      \"acc\": 0.001,\r\n    97\t      \"event\": \"step\",\r\n    98\t      \"sources\": [\"shard_001.jsonl\"],\r\n    99\t      \"conflict\": false\r\n   100\t    }\r\n   101\t  ]\r\n   102\t}\r\n   103\t```\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\t**Field rules:**\r\n"]
[5453.512072, "o", "   106\t- `entries`: sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   107\t- `sources`: list of shard filenames (basenames) that contained this `(epoch, step)`.\r\n"]
[5453.512132, "o", "   108\t- `conflict`: `true` if this entry was chosen by conflict resolution.\r\n   109\t- `gaps`: only gaps where `gap_steps > 100` within the same epoch.\r\n   110\t- Entries with missing optional fields omit them from the JSON (do not include null).\r\n   111\t\r\n   112\t---\r\n   113\t\r\n   114\t## 3. Verify Output\r\n   115\t\r\n   116\t```json\r\n   117\t{\r\n   118\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   119\t  \"checkpoints\": [\r\n   120\t    {\r\n   121\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n"]
[5453.512197, "o", "   122\t      \"valid\": true,\r\n   123\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n   124\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": true,\r\n   125\t      \"signature_valid\": null,\r\n   126\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   127\t      \"issues\": []\r\n   128\t    },\r\n   129\t    {\r\n   130\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   131\t      \"valid\": false,\r\n   132\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n"]
[5453.512255, "o", "   133\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": false,\r\n   134\t      \"signature_valid\": true,\r\n   135\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   136\t      \"issues\": [\r\n   137\t        {\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\"}\r\n   138\t      ]\r\n   139\t    }\r\n   140\t  ],\r\n"]
[5453.51232, "o", "   141\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   142\t    \"total\": 3,\r\n   143\t    \"valid\": 2,\r\n   144\t    \"invalid\": 1\r\n   145\t  }\r\n   146\t}\r\n   147\t```\r\n   148\t\r\n   149\t**Field rules:**\r\n   150\t- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n   151\t- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\n"]
[5453.512387, "o", "   152\t- `issues`: list of issue objects with `type` (string) and `detail` (string). For example, a tensor checksum mismatch appears as `{\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"<tensor_name>\"}`.\r\n   153\t- `valid`: `true` only if all applicable checks pass.\r\n   154\t\r\n   155\t---\r\n   156\t\r\n   157"]
[5453.512449, "o", "\t## 4. Detect Output\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t```json\r\n   160\t{\r\n   161\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   162\t  \"anomalies\": [\r\n   163\t    {\r\n   164\t      \"id\": \"ANOM-001\",\r\n   165\t      \"type\": \"gradient_spike\",\r\n   166\t      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\n   167\t      \"epoch\": 2,\r\n   168\t      \"step\": 3456,\r\n   169\t      \"details\": {\r\n   170\t        \"observed\": 15.3,\r\n"]
[5453.512511, "o", "   171\t        \"window_mean\": 1.2,\r\n   172\t        \"window_stddev\": 0.3,\r\n   173\t        \"z_score\": 47.0\r\n   174\t      },\r\n   175\t      \"evidence\": {\r\n   176\t        \"window_values\": [1.1, 1.3, 1.0, 1.2, 1.4]\r\n   177\t      },\r\n   178\t      \"source\": \"shard_002.jsonl\"\r\n   179\t    },\r\n   180"]
[5453.512568, "o", "\t    {\r\n   181\t      \"id\": \"ANOM-002\",\r\n   182\t      \"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\",\r\n   183\t      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\n   184\t      \"details\": {\r\n   185\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   186\t        \"tensor_name\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\",\r\n   187\t        \"expected_checksum\": \"abcd1234...\",\r\n   188\t        \"actual_checksum\": \"efgh5678...\"\r\n"]
[5453.512625, "o", "   189\t      },\r\n   190\t      \"evidence\": {},\r\n   191\t      \"source\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   192\t      \"checkpoint\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\"\r\n   193\t    }\r\n   194\t  ],\r\n   195\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   196\t    \"total\": 5,\r\n"]
[5453.512686, "o", "   197\t    \"by_severity\": {\r\n   198\t      \"critical\": 1,\r\n   199\t      \"high\": 2,\r\n   200\t      \"medium\": 1,\r\n   201\t      \"low\": 1\r\n   202\t    },\r\n   203\t    \"by_type\": {\r\n   204\t      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n   205\t      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n   206\t      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n"]
[5453.512752, "o", "   207\t      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n   208\t      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n   209\t    }\r\n   210\t  }\r\n   211\t}\r\n   212\t```\r\n   213\t\r\n   214\t**Field rules:**\r\n   215\t- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n"]
[5453.512817, "o", "   216\t- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\r\n   217\t- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n   218\t- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n   219\t- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\n   220\t- `source`: the artifact file "]
[5453.512888, "o", "where the anomaly was detected.\r\n   221\t- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\r\n   222\t- `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\r\n   223\t- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\r\n   224\t- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n   225\t\r\n   226\t### Detect CSV Output\r\n   227\t\r\n   228\tWhen `--format csv` is used with `detect`, the command outputs CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly:\r\n   229\t\r\n   230\t```text\r\n   231\tid,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\r\n   232\t```\r\n   233\t\r\n"]
[5453.512973, "o", "   234\tOne header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\n   235\t\r\n   236\t---\r\n   237\t\r\n   238\t## 5. Lineage Output\r\n   239\t\r\n   240\t```json\r\n   241\t{\r\n   242\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   243\t  \"nodes\": [\r\n   244\t    {\r\n   245\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n"]
[5453.513005, "o", "   246\t      \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n   247\t      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n"]
[5453.513156, "o", "   248\t      \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n   249\t      \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n   250\t      \"parent_hash\": \"\",\r\n   251\t      \"is_root\": true,\r\n   252\t      \"is_leaf\": false,\r\n   253\t      \"is_orphan\": false\r\n   254\t    }\r\n   255\t  ],\r\n   256\t  \"edges\": [\r\n   257\t    {\r\n   258\t      \"from\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n   259\t      \"to\": \"d4e5f6...\",\r\n   260\t      \"from_file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n"]
[5453.513669, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5453.513727, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[5453.792654, "i", "nl -ba internal/forensics/detect.go | sed -n '1,140p'\n"]
[5453.79309, "o", "nl -ba internal/forensics/detect.go | sed -n '1,140p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5453.796685, "o", "     1\tpackage forensics\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\timport (\r\n     4\t\t\"crypto/hmac\"\r\n     5\t\t\"crypto/sha256\"\r\n"]
[5453.796813, "o", "     6\t\t\"encoding/binary\"\r\n     7\t\t\"encoding/hex\"\r\n     8\t\t\"fmt\"\r\n     9\t\t\"hash/fnv\"\r\n    10\t\t\"math\"\r\n    11\t\t\"os\"\r\n    12\t\t\"sort\"\r\n    13\t\t\"time\"\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\t\t\"mlforge/internal/checkpoint\"\r\n    16\t\t\"mlforge/internal/types\"\r\n    17\t)\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tfunc loadCheckpoints(dir string) ([]*types.CheckpointFile, error) {\r\n    20\t\tap, err := DiscoverArtifacts(dir)\r\n    21\t\tif err != nil {\r\n    22\t\t\treturn nil, err\r\n    23\t\t}\r\n    24\t\tvar cps []*types.CheckpointFile\r\n    25\t"]
[5453.796903, "o", "\tfor _, p := range ap.Checkpoints {\r\n    26\t\t\tcf, err := checkpoint.Parse(p)\r\n    27\t\t\tif err != nil || cf == nil {\r\n    28\t\t\t\tcontinue\r\n    29\t\t\t}\r\n    30\t\t\tcps = append(cps, cf)\r\n    31\t\t}\r\n    32\t\tsort.Slice(cps, func(i, j int) bool {\r\n    33\t\t\treturn cps[i].Filename < cps[j].Filename\r\n    34\t\t})\r\n    35\t\treturn cps, nil\r\n"]
[5453.797022, "o", "    36\t}\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\ttype DetectOutput struct {\r\n    39\t\tStatus    string          `json:\"status\"`\r\n    40\t\tAnomalies []types.Anomaly `json:\"anomalies\"`\r\n    41\t\tSummary   struct {\r\n    42\t\t\tTotal      int            `json:\"total\"`\r\n    43\t\t\tBySeverity map[string]int `json:\"by_severity\"`\r\n    44\t\t\tByType     map[string]int `json:\"by_type\"`\r\n    45\t\t} `json:\"summary\"`\r\n    46\t}\r\n    47\t\r\n    48\tfunc BuildDetect(dir string) (interface{}, error) {\r\n    49\t\treturn BuildDetectFiltered(dir, \"\")\r\n    50\t}\r\n    51\t\r\n    52\t"]
[5453.797103, "o", "func BuildDetectFiltered(dir, filterSeverity string) (DetectOutput, error) {\r\n    53\t\tvar out DetectOutput\r\n    54\t\tout.Status = \"ok\"\r\n    55\t\tvar anomalies []types.Anomaly\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t\tentries, _, err := loadTimelineEntries(dir)\r\n    58\t\tif err == nil {\r\n    59\t\t\tmerged, _ := mergeTimeline(entries)\r\n    60\t\t\tsortTimeline(merged)\r\n    61\t\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectTimelineAnomalies(merged)...)\r\n    62\t\t}\r\n    63\t\r\n"]
[5453.79718, "o", "    64\t\tcps, err := loadCheckpoints(dir)\r\n    65\t\tif err == nil {\r\n    66\t\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectCheckpointAnomalies(dir, cps)...)\r\n    67\t\t}\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t\tif filterSeverity != \"\" {\r\n    70\t"]
[5453.797245, "o", "\t\twantedRank, ok := severityRankValue(filterSeverity)\r\n    71\t\t\tif !ok {\r\n    72\t\t\t\treturn out, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid severity level %q: must be critical, high, medium, or low\", filterSeverity)\r\n    73\t\t\t}\r\n    74\t\t\tfiltered := anomalies[:0]\r\n    75\t\t\tfor _, a := range anomalies {\r\n    76\t\t\t\tif severityRank(a.Severity) <= wantedRank {\r\n    77\t\t\t\t\tfiltered = append(filtered, a)\r\n    78\t\t\t\t}\r\n    79\t\t\t}\r\n    80\t\t\tanomalies = filtered\r\n    81\t\t}\r\n    82\t\r\n    83\t\tfor i := range anomalies {\r\n    84\t\t\tanomalies[i].ID = fmt.Sprintf(\"ANOM-%03d\", i+1)\r\n"]
[5453.797305, "o", "    85\t\t}\r\n    86\t\tsortAnomalies(anomalies)\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t\tout.Anomalies = anomalies\r\n    89\t\tif out.Anomalies == nil {\r\n    90\t\t\tout.Anomalies = []types.Anomaly{}\r\n    91\t\t}\r\n    92\t\tout.Summary.Total = len(anomalies)\r\n    93\t\tout.Summary.BySeverity = map[string]int{\"critical\": 0, \"high\": 0, \"medium\": 0, \"low\": 0}\r\n    94"]
[5453.797364, "o", "\t\tout.Summary.ByType = map[string]int{}\r\n    95\t\tfor _, a := range anomalies {\r\n    96\t\t\tout.Summary.BySeverity[a.Severity]++\r\n    97\t\t\tout.Summary.ByType[a.Type]++\r\n    98\t\t}\r\n    99\t\treturn out, nil\r\n   100\t}\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\tfunc severityRank(s string) int {\r\n"]
[5453.797421, "o", "   103\t\tswitch s {\r\n   104\t\tcase \"critical\":\r\n   105\t\t\treturn 0\r\n   106\t\tcase \"high\":\r\n   107\t\t\treturn 1\r\n   108\t\tcase \"medium\":\r\n   109\t\t\treturn 2\r\n   110\t\tdefault:\r\n"]
[5453.797478, "o", "   111\t\t\treturn 3\r\n   112\t\t}\r\n   113\t}\r\n   114\t\r\n   115\tfunc severityRankValue(s string) (int, bool) {\r\n   116\t\tswitch s {\r\n   117\t\tcase \"critical\":\r\n   118\t\t\treturn 0, true\r\n   119\t\tcase \"high\":\r\n   120\t\t\treturn 1, true\r\n   121"]
[5453.797536, "o", "\t\tcase \"medium\":\r\n   122\t\t\treturn 2, true\r\n   123\t\tcase \"low\":\r\n   124\t\t\treturn 3, true\r\n   125\t\tdefault:\r\n   126\t\t\treturn 4, false\r\n   127\t\t}\r\n   128\t}\r\n   129\t\r\n"]
[5453.797592, "o", "   130\tfunc detectTimelineAnomalies(entries []types.TimelineEntry) []types.Anomaly {\r\n   131\t\tvar anomalies []types.Anomaly\r\n   132\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectGradientSpikes(entries)...)\r\n   133\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectLossDivergence(entries)...)\r\n   134\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectLrAnomalies(entries)...)\r\n   135\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectTrainingGaps(entries)...)\r\n"]
[5453.79765, "o", "   136\t\tanomalies = append(anomalies, detectMetricRegression(entries)...)\r\n   137\t\treturn anomalies\r\n   138\t}\r\n   139\t\r\n   140\tfunc detectGradientSpikes(entries []types.TimelineEntry) []types.Anomaly {\r\n"]
