[5798.650031, "o", "docs/analysis_rules.md:7:Given multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:14:4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:29:Anomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`.\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:36:- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:45:- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:51:- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:55:- **Severity**: `medium`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:60:- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:62:- **Severity**: `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:69:- **Severity**: `critical`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:76:- **Severity**: `critical`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:83:- **Severity**: `critical`\r\ndocs"]
[5798.650141, "o", "/analysis_rules.md:90:- **Severity**: `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:95:- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:97:- **Severity**: `low`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:104:- **Severity**: `high`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:130:- `NOT` is a prefix operator with the highest precedence.\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:151:JSON array of matching timeline entries (after reconstruction), sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:181:The lineage output includes a topological ordering of all non-orphan nodes, from root to leaf. If multiple valid orderings exist, sort by `CreationTimestamp` ascending as tiebreaker.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:59:- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:60:- `log_shards` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:61:- `configs` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:106:- `entries`: sorted by `(epoch AS"]
[5798.650211, "o", "C, step ASC)`.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:150:- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:166:      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:183:      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:197:    \"by_severity\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:198:      \"critical\": 1,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:199:      \"high\": 2,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:200:      \"medium\": 1,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:201:      \"info\": 1\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:207:      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:208:      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:216:- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (`critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`), then `type` alphabetically, then `epoch` ascending, then `step` ascending.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:217:- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:219:- `ev"]
[5798.650273, "o", "idence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:223:- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:231:id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:234:One header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before"]
[5798.650336, "o", " CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:273:- `nodes`: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:274:- `edges`: sorted by `from` hash then `to` hash lexicographically.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:275:- `roots`: file hashes of root nodes (no parent), sorted.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:276:- `leaves`: file hashes of leaf nodes (no children), sorted.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:277:- `orphans`: file hashes of orphan nodes (parent not found), sorted.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:278:- `topological_order`: valid topological sort of non-orphan nodes, ties broken by `creation_timestamp`.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:331:- `entries`: matching timeline entries sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:378:- `tensor_diffs`: sorted by tensor name lexicographically.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:385:- `summary.only_in_a` and `summary.only_in_b`: tensor names present in only one file, sorted lexicographically.\r\n"]
