[5853.378914, "o", "grep -n \"filter-severity\\|critical > high\\|Severity order\" docs/output_schema.md docs/spec.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5853.382164, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K223\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K` is supplied.\r\n"]
[5853.382274, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/output_schema.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K234\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[KOne header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\n"]
[5853.382465, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[Kdocs/spec.md\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32m\u001b[K80\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K- `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the specified severity level or above. \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KSeverity order\u001b[m\u001b[K is `\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kcritical > high\u001b[m\u001b[K > medium > low`. For example, `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K high` shows only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kfilter-severity\u001b[m\u001b[K critical` shows only `critical` anomalies. The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.\r\n"]
[5853.382956, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
