[5868.888011, "o", "# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n\r\n## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n\r\n"]
[5868.888121, "o", "Given multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n\r\n1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **earliest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n\r\nAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing which shard files contai"]
[5868.888201, "o", "ned this `(epoch, step)`\r\n- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n\r\nAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`.\r\n\r\n"]
[5868.888685, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5868.888747, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[5869.159419, "i", "sed -n '70,90p' docs/spec.md\n"]
[5869.159771, "o", "sed -n '70,90p' docs/spec.md\r\n"]
[5869.159886, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5869.162702, "o", "\r\nRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n"]
[5869.162804, "o", "- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n\r\n"]
[5869.162874, "o", "Every anomaly object includes a top-level `evidence` field. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values` with up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies have an empty `evidence` object.\r\n\r\nDetect-specific flags:\r\n- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.\r\n- `--filter-severity LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the specified severity level or above. Severity order is `critical > high > medium > low`. For example, `--filter-severity high` shows only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--filter-severity critical` shows only `critical` anomalies. "]
[5869.162983, "o", "The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.\r\n\r\nOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n\r\n#### `lineage`\r\n\r\nBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n\r\n**Rules**:\r\n- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n"]
[5869.163318, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5869.163379, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[5881.138077, "i", "nl -ba docs/analysis_rules.md | sed -n '25,115p'\n"]
[5881.138468, "o", "nl -ba docs/analysis_rules.md | sed -n '25,115p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5881.142335, "o", "    25\t---\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    34\t- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n    35\t- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n"]
[5881.142582, "o", "    36\t- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n    37\t- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n    38\t- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n    41\t\r\n    42\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    43\t- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n    44\t- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n    45\t- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n    46\t- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n    47\t- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n    52\t- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n    53\t  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end"]
[5881.14269, "o", "` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n    54\t  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n    55\t- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n    56\t- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n    61\t- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n    62\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    63\t- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n    68\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    69\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    70\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    71\t\r\n    72\t### 2.6 Checkpoint I"]
[5881.142763, "o", "ntegrity - Header Checksum\r\n    73\t\r\n    74\t- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n    75\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    76\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    77\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n    80\t\r\n"]
[5881.14283, "o", "    81\t- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n    82\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    83\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    84\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n    85\t\r\n    86\t### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set"]
[5881.142888, "o", "\r\n    89\t- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n    90\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    91\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n    92\t\r\n    93\t### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n    94\t"]
[5881.143013, "o", "\r\n    95\t- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n    96\t- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n    97\t- **Severity**: `low`\r\n    98\t- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n    99\t\r\n   100\t### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\t- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n   103\t- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n   104\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n"]
[5881.143075, "o", "   105\t- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n   106\t\r\n   107\t---\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t## 3. Query Language\r\n   110\t\r\n   111\t### 3.1 Grammar\r\n"]
[5881.143146, "o", "   112\t\r\n   113\t```\r\n   114\tquery      := or_expr\r\n   115\tor_expr    := and_expr (\"OR\" and_expr)*\r\n"]
