[5962.222435, "o", "sed -n '150,236p' docs/output_schema.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5962.225532, "o", "- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\n- `issues`: list of issue objects with `type` (string) and `detail` (string). For example, a tensor checksum mismatch appears as `{\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"<tensor_name>\"}`.\r\n- `valid`: `true` only if all applicable checks pass.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Detect Output\r\n\r\n```json"]
[5962.225653, "o", "\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"anomalies\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"ANOM-001\",\r\n      \"type\": \"gradient_spike\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\n      \"epoch\": 2,\r\n      \"step\": 3456,\r\n      \"details\": {\r\n        \"observed\": 15.3,\r\n        \"window_mean\": 1.2,\r\n        \"window_stddev\": 0.3,\r\n        \"z_score\": 47.0\r\n      },\r\n      \"evidence\": {\r\n        \"window_values\": [1.1, 1.3, 1.0, 1.2, 1.4]\r\n      },\r\n      \"source\": \"shard_002.jsonl\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"ANOM-002\",\r\n"]
[5962.225731, "o", "      \"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\n      \"details\": {\r\n        \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n        \"tensor_name\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\",\r\n        \"expected_checksum\": \"abcd1234...\",\r\n        \"actual_checksum\": \"efgh5678...\"\r\n      },\r\n"]
[5962.225794, "o", "      \"evidence\": {},\r\n      \"source\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n      \"checkpoint\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"total\": 5,\r\n    \"by_severity\": {\r\n      \"critical\": 1,\r\n      \"high\": 2,\r\n      \"medium\": 1,\r\n      \"info\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"by_type\": {\r\n      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n    }\r\n"]
[5962.225859, "o", "  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (`critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`), then `type` alphabetically, then `epoch` ascending, then `step` ascending.\r\n- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n"]
[5962.225926, "o", "- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\n- `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.\r\n- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\r\n- `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\r\n- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\r\n- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n\r\n### Detect CSV Output\r\n\r\nWhen `--for"]
[5962.226032, "o", "mat csv` is used with `detect`, the command outputs CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nid,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\r\n```\r\n\r\nOne header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\n\r\n---\r\n"]
[5962.226506, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
