[5987.52005, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[5987.520321, "o", "sed -n '150,236p' docs/output_schema.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5987.523285, "o", "- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\n- `issues`: list of issue objects with `type` (string) and `detail` (string). For example, a tensor checksum mismatch appears as `{\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"<tensor_name>\"}`.\r\n- `valid`: `true` only if all applicable checks pass.\r\n\r\n---\r\n"]
[5987.523362, "o", "\r\n## 4. Detect Output\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n  \"anomalies\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"ANOM-001\",\r\n      \"type\": \"gradient_spike\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\n      \"epoch\": 2,\r\n      \"step\": 3456,\r\n      \"details\": {\r\n"]
[5987.523425, "o", "        \"observed\": 15.3,\r\n        \"window_mean\": 1.2,\r\n        \"window_stddev\": 0.3,\r\n        \"z_score\": 47.0\r\n      },\r\n      \"evidence\": {\r\n        \"window_values\": [1.1, 1.3, 1.0, 1.2, 1.4]\r\n      },\r\n      \"source\": \"shard_002.jsonl\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"ANOM-002\",\r\n      \"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\",\r\n"]
[5987.523487, "o", "      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\n      \"details\": {\r\n        \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n        \"tensor_name\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\",\r\n        \"expected_checksum\": \"abcd1234...\",\r\n        \"actual_checksum\": \"efgh5678...\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"evidence\": {},\r\n      \"source\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n      \"checkpoint\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"total\": 5,\r\n    \"by_severity\": {\r\n"]
[5987.523546, "o", "      \"critical\": 1,\r\n      \"high\": 2,\r\n      \"medium\": 1,\r\n      \"info\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"by_type\": {\r\n      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n    }\r\n"]
[5987.523609, "o", "  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field rules:**\r\n- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (`critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`), then `type` alphabetically, then `epoch` ascending, then `step` ascending.\r\n- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n"]
[5987.523673, "o", "- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\n- `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.\r\n- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\r\n- `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\r\n- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\r\n- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\r\n\r\n### Detect CSV Output\r\n\r\nWhen `--for"]
[5987.523743, "o", "mat csv` is used with `detect`, the command outputs CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nid,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\r\n```\r\n\r\nOne header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\r\n\r\n---\r\n"]
[5987.524255, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5987.52432, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[5987.524527, "o", "sed -n '25,105p' docs/analysis_rules.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5987.527272, "o", "---\r\n\r\n## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n\r\n"]
[5987.527343, "o", "Anomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`.\r\n\r\n### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n\r\n- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n\r\n### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n\r\n- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n"]
[5987.527416, "o", "- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n\r\n### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n"]
[5987.527479, "o", "  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n- **Severity**: `info`\r\n- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n\r\n### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n\r\n- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n\r\n### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n\r\n"]
[5987.527544, "o", "### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n\r\n### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n\r\n"]
[5987.527643, "o", "### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n\r\n- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\n- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n\r\n### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n- **Severity**: `info`\r\n- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n\r\n### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n\r\n- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n"]
[5987.527706, "o", "- **Severity**: `high`\r\n- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n"]
[5987.528115, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5987.528173, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[5987.621141, "i", "grep -R \"critical > high > medium > low > info\\|by_severity\\|info\" -n docs/analysis_rules.md docs/output_schema.md internal/forensics/detect.go | head -120\n"]
[5987.62185, "o", "grep -R \"critical > high > medium > low > info\\|by_severity\\|info\" -n docs/analysis_rules.md docs/output_schema.md internal/forensics/detect.go | head -120\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5987.626052, "o", "docs/analysis_rules.md:29:Anomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`.\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:55:- **Severity**: `info`\r\ndocs/analysis_rules.md:97:- **Severity**: `info`\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:197:    \"by_severity\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:201:      \"info\": 1\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:216:- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (`critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`), then `type` alphabetically, then `epoch` ascending, then `step` ascending.\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:43:\t\tBySeverity map[string]int `json:\"by_severity\"`\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:72:\t\t\treturn out, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid severity level %q: must be critical, high, medium, low, or info\", filterSeverity)\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:112:\tcase \"info\":\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:128:\tcase \"info\":\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:255:\t\t\t\tSeverity: \"info\",\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:290:\t\t\t\tSeverity: \"info\",\r\ninternal/forensics/detect.go:614:\trank := map[string]int{\"critical\": 0, \"high\": 1, \"medium\": 2, "]
[5987.626145, "o", "\"low\": 3, \"info\": 4}\r\n"]
