[6181.702011, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[6181.705728, "o", "     1\t# Analysis Rules and Query Language\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## 1. Timeline Reconstruction\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t### 1.1 Merge Algorithm\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\tGiven multiple `.jsonl` shard files, the timeline is reconstructed as follows:\r\n"]
[6181.705841, "o", "     8\t\r\n     9\t1. **Parse**: Read all entries from all shard files. Skip malformed JSON lines.\r\n    10\t2. **Deduplicate**: Entries are keyed by `(epoch, step)`. When multiple entries share the same key:\r\n    11\t   - If all numeric metric values (loss, lr, grad_norm, acc) are identical (within 1e-9 tolerance), keep one copy.\r\n    12\t   - If values differ, this is a **conflict**. Resolution: keep the entry with the **earliest** `ts` timestamp. Record the conflict.\r\n    13\t3. **Sort**: Sort the unified timeline by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n    14\t4. **Gap Detection**: A gap exists when consecutive entries (after sorting) satisfy:\r\n    15\t   - Same epoch: `step_diff = next.step - curr.step > 1` AND `step_diff > 100`\r\n    16\t   - Cross-epoch boundary: not a gap (step resets are normal at epoch boundaries)\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t### 1.2 Timeline Entry Output\r\n    19\t\r\n    20\tAfter merge, each entry in the timeline has:\r\n    21\t- All original fields from the winning entry\r\n    22\t- An additional `\"sources\"` array listing"]
[6181.705925, "o", " which shard files contained this `(epoch, step)`\r\n    23\t- If this entry was a conflict resolution, an additional `\"conflict\": true` field\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\t---\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## 2. Anomaly Detection Rules\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tAnomalies are classified by severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`.\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\tSeverity order, from most severe to least severe, is `critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`. Anomalies are sorted by severity, then `type` alphabetically, then `epoch` ascending, then `step` ascending.\r\n    32\t\r\n    33\t### 2.1 Gradient Norm Spike\r\n    34\t\r\n"]
[6181.706009, "o", "    35\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    36\t- **Method**: Compute mean and standard deviation of `grad_norm` over the window\r\n    37\t- **Trigger**: `grad_norm > mean + 3.0 * stddev` (Z-score > 3.0)\r\n    38\t- **Severity**: `high` if Z-score > 5.0, else `medium`\r\n    39\t- **Required data**: At least 50 entries with `grad_norm` before detection begins\r\n    40\t- **Output fields**: `observed`, `window_mean`, `window_stddev`, `z_score`\r\n    41\t\r\n    42\t### 2.2 Loss Divergence\r\n    43\t\r\n"]
[6181.706074, "o", "    44\t- **Window**: Sliding window of 50 steps\r\n    45\t- **Method**: Compare loss at window start vs window end\r\n    46\t- **Trigger**: `(loss_end - loss_start) / |loss_start| > 1.0` (>100% increase)\r\n    47\t- **Severity**: `critical` if increase > 5.0 (500%), else `high`\r\n    48\t- **Guard**: Only trigger if `|loss_start| > 1e-6` (avoid division by near-zero)\r\n    49\t- **Output fields**: `loss_start`, `loss_end`, `increase_ratio`, `window_start_step`, `window_end_step`\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t### 2.3 Learning Rate Anomaly\r\n    52\t\r\n"]
[6181.706137, "o", "    53\t- **Method**: Analyze the sequence of `lr` values across sorted timeline\r\n    54\t- **Trigger**: `lr` increases between consecutive entries UNLESS:\r\n    55\t  - The increase coincides with an `epoch_end` event (warmup restart pattern)\r\n    56\t  - The increase is the first entry (no previous to compare)\r\n    57\t- **Severity**: `info`\r\n    58\t- **Output fields**: `prev_lr`, `curr_lr`, `step`\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t### 2.4 Metric Regression\r\n"]
[6181.706199, "o", "    61\t\r\n    62\t- **Scope**: Between consecutive checkpoints (entries with `event == \"checkpoint\"` or between .mlck files sorted by epoch/step)\r\n    63\t- **Trigger**: `acc` drops by more than 0.15 (absolute, not relative) between consecutive checkpoints\r\n    64\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n    65\t- **Output fields**: `prev_acc`, `curr_acc`, `drop`, `prev_checkpoint`, `curr_checkpoint`\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t### 2.5 Checkpoint Integrity - Tensor Checksum\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t- **Method**: For each tensor in a `.mlck` file, compute SHA-256 of the data bytes and compare with stored checksum\r\n"]
[6181.706256, "o", "    70\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    71\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    72\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `tensor_name`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    73\t\r\n    74\t### 2.6 Checkpoint Integrity - Header Checksum\r\n    75\t\r\n"]
[6181.706322, "o", "    76\t- **Method**: Compute FNV-1a 64-bit of bytes [0..48) and compare with stored value at offset 48\r\n    77\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    78\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n    79\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `expected_checksum` (hex), `actual_checksum` (hex)\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\t### 2.7 Checkpoint Integrity - Signature\r\n    82\t\r\n    83\t- **Method**: For signed checkpoints (Flags bit 0), compute HMAC-SHA256 of bytes [0..SignatureOffset) using SignerId as key, compare with stored signature\r\n    84\t- **Trigger**: Mismatch\r\n    85\t- **Severity**: `critical`\r\n"]
[6181.706383, "o", "    86\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `signer_id`, `valid` (bool)\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t### 2.8 Provenance Chain Break\r\n    89\t\r\n    90\t- **Method**: For each checkpoint with a non-empty `parent_hash`, verify that a checkpoint with that file hash exists in the evidence set\r\n    91\t- **Trigger**: Parent checkpoint not found\r\n    92\t- **Severity**: `medium`\r\n    93\t- **Output fields**: `file`, `parent_hash`, `found` (bool)\r\n    94\t\r\n    95\t### 2.9 Training Gap\r\n    96\t\r\n    97\t"]
[6181.706453, "o", "- **Method**: Consecutive timeline entries (after merge sort) have timestamps more than 2 hours apart\r\n    98\t- **Trigger**: `time_diff > 7200 seconds` between consecutive entries within the same epoch\r\n    99\t- **Severity**: `info`\r\n   100\t- **Output fields**: `after_step`, `before_step`, `after_ts`, `before_ts`, `gap_seconds`\r\n   101\t\r\n"]
[6181.706515, "o", "   102\t### 2.10 Dataset Hash Inconsistency\r\n   103\t\r\n   104\t- **Method**: Compare `DatasetHash` across all checkpoints in the same lineage chain\r\n   105\t- **Trigger**: Different `DatasetHash` values within the same chain\r\n   106\t- **Severity**: `high`\r\n   107\t- **Output fields**: `files`, `hashes` (list of unique hex hashes)\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t---\r\n   110\t\r\n   111\t## 3. Query Language\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t### 3.1 Grammar\r\n   114\t\r\n   115\t```\r\n   116\tquery      := or_expr\r\n   117\tor_expr    := and_expr (\"OR\" and_expr)*\r\n"]
[6181.706577, "o", "   118\tand_expr   := not_expr (\"AND\" not_expr)*\r\n   119\tnot_expr   := \"NOT\" not_expr | atom\r\n   120\tatom       := \"(\" or_expr \")\" | condition\r\n"]
[6181.70716, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
