[7802.532048, "o", "     1\t# Output Schemas\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tAll commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\r\n     4\t\r\n     5"]
[7802.532188, "o", "\t---\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## 1. Ingest Output\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t```json\r\n    10\t{\r\n    11\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    12\t  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\r\n    13\t  \"artifacts\": {\r\n    14\t    \"checkpoints\": [\r\n    15\t      {\r\n    16\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n    17\t        \"file_hash\": \"a1b2c3...\",\r\n    18\t        \"version\": 1,\r\n    19\t        \"num_tensors\": 12,\r\n    20\t        \"num_metadata\": 3,\r\n    21\t        \"signed\": false,\r\n    22\t        \"creation_timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    23\t        \"provenance\": {\r\n    24\t          \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    25\t          \"global_step\": 5000,\r\n    26\t          \"framework\": \"PyTorch\",\r\n    27\t          \"framework_version\": \"2.1.0\",\r\n    28\t          \"parent_hash\": \"\"\r\n    29\t        }\r\n    30\t      }"]
[7802.532271, "o", "\r\n    31\t    ],\r\n    32\t    \"log_shards\": [\r\n    33\t      {\r\n    34\t        \"file\": \"shard_001.jsonl\",\r\n    35\t        \"entries\": 500,\r\n    36\t        \"step_range\": [0, 5000],\r\n    37\t        \"epoch_range\": [0, 1],\r\n    38\t        \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\"]\r\n    39\t      }\r\n    40\t    ],\r\n    41\t    \"configs\": [\r\n    42\t      {\r\n    43\t        \"file\": \"config_train.json\",\r\n    44\t        \"model_name\": \"resnet50\",\r\n    45\t        \"dataset\": \"imagenet-1k\"\r\n"]
[7802.532336, "o", "    46\t      }\r\n    47\t    ]\r\n    48\t  },\r\n    49\t  \"totals\": {\r\n    50\t    \"checkpoints\": 3,\r\n    51\t    \"log_shards\": 4,\r\n    52\t    \"configs\": 1\r\n    53\t  }\r\n    54\t}\r\n    55\t```\r\n    56\t\r\n    57\t**Field rules:**\r\n"]
[7802.532401, "o", "    58\t- `file_hash`: SHA-256 hex of the entire `.mlck` file content.\r\n    59\t- `checkpoints` array: sorted by `creation_timestamp` ascending.\r\n    60\t- `log_shards` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    61\t- `configs` array: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n    62\t- `step_range`: `[min_step, max_step]` across all entries in the shard.\r\n    63\t- `epoch_range`: `[min_epoch, max_epoch]` across all entries.\r\n    64\t- `time_range`: `[earliest_ts, latest_ts]` as ISO 8601 strings.\r\n    65\t\r\n    66\t---\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\t## 2. Timeline Output\r\n"]
[7802.532461, "o", "    69\t\r\n    70\t```json\r\n    71\t{\r\n    72\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n    73\t  \"total_entries\": 1200,\r\n    74\t  \"total_epochs\": 5,\r\n    75\t  \"step_range\": [0, 50000],\r\n    76\t  \"time_range\": [\"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\", \"2024-01-17T14:00:00Z\"],\r\n    77\t  \"conflicts_resolved\": 3,\r\n    78\t  \"gaps\": [\r\n    79\t    {\r\n"]
[7802.532523, "o", "    80\t      \"after_step\": 5000,\r\n    81\t      \"before_step\": 5200,\r\n    82\t      \"epoch\": 1,\r\n    83\t      \"gap_steps\": 200,\r\n    84\t      \"after_ts\": \"2024-01-15T10:00:00Z\",\r\n    85\t      \"before_ts\": \"2024-01-15T13:00:00Z\"\r\n    86\t    }\r\n    87\t  ],\r\n    88\t  \"entries\": [\r\n    89\t    {\r\n"]
[7802.532582, "o", "    90\t      \"ts\": \"2024-01-15T08:00:00Z\",\r\n    91\t      \"epoch\": 0,\r\n    92\t      \"step\": 0,\r\n    93\t      \"loss\": 6.9078,\r\n    94\t      \"lr\": 0.001,\r\n    95\t      \"grad_norm\": 12.34,\r\n    96\t      \"acc\": 0.001,\r\n    97\t      \"event\": \"step\",\r\n    98\t      \"sources\": [\"shard_001.jsonl\"],\r\n    99\t      \"conflict\": false\r\n   100\t    }\r\n   101\t  ]\r\n"]
[7802.532644, "o", "   102\t}\r\n   103\t```\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\t**Field rules:**\r\n   106\t- `entries`: sorted by `(epoch ASC, step ASC)`.\r\n   107\t- `sources`: list of shard filenames (basenames) that contained this `(epoch, step)`.\r\n   108\t- `conflict`: `true` if this entry was chosen by conflict resolution.\r\n   109\t- `gaps`: only gaps where `gap_steps > 100` within the same epoch.\r\n   110\t- Entries with missing optional fields omit them from the JSON (do not include null).\r\n   111\t\r\n   112\t---\r\n"]
[7802.532701, "o", "   113\t\r\n   114\t## 3. Verify Output\r\n   115\t\r\n   116\t```json\r\n   117\t{\r\n   118\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   119\t  \"checkpoints\": [\r\n   120\t    {\r\n   121\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch1.mlck\",\r\n   122\t      \"valid\": true,\r\n"]
[7802.532761, "o", "   123\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n   124\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": true,\r\n   125\t      \"signature_valid\": null,\r\n   126\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   127\t      \"issues\": []\r\n   128\t    },\r\n   129\t    {\r\n   130\t      \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   131\t      \"valid\": false,\r\n   132"]
[7802.532834, "o", "\t      \"header_checksum_valid\": true,\r\n   133\t      \"tensor_checksums_valid\": false,\r\n   134\t      \"signature_valid\": true,\r\n   135\t      \"provenance_valid\": true,\r\n   136\t      \"issues\": [\r\n   137\t        {\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\"}\r\n   138\t      ]\r\n   139\t    }\r\n   140\t  ],\r\n   141\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   142\t    \"total\": 3,\r\n"]
[7802.532899, "o", "   143\t    \"valid\": 2,\r\n   144\t    \"invalid\": 1\r\n   145\t  }\r\n   146\t}\r\n   147\t```\r\n   148\t\r\n   149\t**Field rules:**\r\n   150\t- `checkpoints`: sorted by `file` name lexicographically.\r\n   151\t- `signature_valid`: `null` if the checkpoint is unsigned, `true`/`false` if signed.\r\n   152\t"]
[7802.532994, "o", "- `issues`: list of issue objects with `type` (string) and `detail` (string). For example, a tensor checksum mismatch appears as `{\"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\", \"detail\": \"<tensor_name>\"}`.\r\n   153\t- `valid`: `true` only if all applicable checks pass.\r\n   154\t\r\n   155\t---\r\n   156\t\r\n   157\t## 4. Detect Output\r\n   158\t\r\n   159\t```json\r\n   160\t{\r\n   161\t  \"status\": \"ok\",\r\n   162\t  \"anomalies\": [\r\n   163\t    {\r\n   164\t      \"id\": \"ANOM-001\",\r\n   165\t      \"type\": \"gradient_spike\",\r\n"]
[7802.533058, "o", "   166\t      \"severity\": \"high\",\r\n   167\t      \"epoch\": 2,\r\n   168\t      \"step\": 3456,\r\n   169\t      \"details\": {\r\n   170\t        \"observed\": 15.3,\r\n   171\t        \"ewma_mean\": 1.2,\r\n   172\t        \"ewma_stddev\": 0.3,\r\n   173\t        \"z_score\": 47.0\r\n   174\t      },\r\n   175\t      \"evidence\": {\r\n   176\t        \"window_values\": [1.1, 1.3, 1.0, 1.2, 1.4]\r\n   177\t      },\r\n"]
[7802.533118, "o", "   178\t      \"source\": \"shard_002.jsonl\"\r\n   179\t    },\r\n   180\t    {\r\n   181\t      \"id\": \"ANOM-002\",\r\n   182\t      \"type\": \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\",\r\n   183\t      \"severity\": \"critical\",\r\n   184\t      \"details\": {\r\n   185\t        \"file\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n"]
[7802.533183, "o", "   186\t        \"tensor_name\": \"encoder.layer2.weight\",\r\n   187\t        \"expected_checksum\": \"abcd1234...\",\r\n   188\t        \"actual_checksum\": \"efgh5678...\"\r\n   189\t      },\r\n   190\t      \"evidence\": {},\r\n   191\t      \"source\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\",\r\n   192\t      \"checkpoint\": \"model_epoch3.mlck\"\r\n   193\t    }\r\n   194\t  ],\r\n   195\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   196\t    \"total\": 5,\r\n"]
[7802.533241, "o", "   197\t    \"by_severity\": {\r\n   198\t      \"critical\": 1,\r\n   199\t      \"high\": 2,\r\n   200\t      \"medium\": 1,\r\n   201\t      \"info\": 1\r\n   202\t    },\r\n   203\t    \"by_type\": {\r\n   204\t      \"gradient_spike\": 1,\r\n"]
[7802.533304, "o", "   205\t      \"loss_divergence\": 1,\r\n   206\t      \"tensor_checksum_mismatch\": 1,\r\n   207\t      \"training_gap\": 1,\r\n   208\t      \"lr_anomaly\": 1\r\n   209\t    }\r\n   210\t  }\r\n   211\t}\r\n   212\t```\r\n   213\t\r\n   214\t**Field rules:**\r\n   215\t- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\r\n   216\t- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (`critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`), then `type` alphabetically, then `epoch` ascending, then `step` ascending.\r\n"]
[7802.533365, "o", "   217\t- Severity order is `critical` > `high` > `medium` > `low` > `info`. `--filter-severity LEVEL` returns anomalies at the specified severity level or above: `critical` returns only `critical`; `high` returns `critical` and `high`; `medium` returns `critical`, `high`, and `medium`; `low` returns `critical`, `high`, `medium`, and `low`; `info` returns all severities.\r\n   218\t- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\r\n"]
[7802.533431, "o", "   219\t- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\r\n   220\t- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\r\n"]
[7802.533968, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
