[7802.816308, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[7802.8203, "o", "     1\t# mlforge - ML Model Artifact Forensics Engine\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\t## Overview\r\n     4\t\r\n"]
[7802.820433, "o", "     5\t`mlforge` is a command-line tool for forensic analysis of machine learning model artifacts. Given a directory of evidence (model checkpoints, training log shards, configuration files), mlforge reconstructs training timelines, detects anomalies, verifies artifact integrity, builds model lineage graphs, and produces evidence-backed forensic reports.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t## CLI Interface\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\tThe binary is built as `mlforge` and placed at `/app/mlforge` (or on `$PATH` after `go install`).\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t```\r\n    12\tmlforge <command> <evidence-dir> [flags]\r\n    13\t```\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\t### Commands\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t| Command | Description |\r\n    18\t|---------|-------------|\r\n    19\t| `ingest` | Scan evidence directory, index all artifacts, print summary to stdout |\r\n    20\t| `timeline` | Reconstruct unified training timeline from log shards |\r\n    21\t| `verify` | Verify integrity of all checkpoint files |\r\n    22\t| `detect` | Run anomaly detection across all evidence |\r\n    23\t| `lineage` | Build "]
[7802.82052, "o", "and output model lineage DAG |\r\n    24\t| `query` | Query the unified timeline with filter expressions |\r\n    25\t| `report` | Generate full forensic report combining all analyses |\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t### Global Flags\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n    30\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n    31\t| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json`, `text`, or `csv` (`csv` is supported only by `detect`) |\r\n    32\t| `--verbose` | bool | false | Enable verbose diagnostic output to stderr |\r\n    33"]
[7802.820589, "o", "\t\r\n    34\t### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\t#### `ingest`\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\tScan `<evidence-dir>` recursively for:\r\n    39\t- `.mlck` files (model checkpoints)\r\n    40\t- `.jsonl` files (training log shards)\r\n    41\t- `.json` files matching `config_*.json` (training configurations)\r\n    42\t\r\n    43\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\tIf the evidence directory does not exist or contains no recognizable artifacts, exit with code 1 and print an error to stderr.\r\n    46\t\r\n    47\t#### `timeline`\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t"]
[7802.82066, "o", "Parse all `.jsonl` log shards in `<evidence-dir>`, merge entries into a unified timeline.\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t**Merge Rules** (detailed in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Timeline Reconstruction\"):\r\n    52\t- Entries are identified by `(epoch, step)` tuple\r\n    53\t- When multiple shards contain the same `(epoch, step)`, apply conflict resolution\r\n    54\t- Gaps in the step sequence are detected and reported\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t#### `verify`\r\n    59\t\r\n"]
[7802.82072, "o", "    60\tFor each `.mlck` file in `<evidence-dir>`:\r\n    61\t1. Parse the file according to the MLCK format (see `/app/docs/formats.md`)\r\n    62\t2. Validate the header checksum\r\n    63\t3. Validate each tensor's SHA-256 data checksum\r\n    64\t4. If the file is signed (Flags bit 0), validate the HMAC-SHA256 signature\r\n    65\t5. Validate provenance fields are well-formed\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n"]
[7802.820785, "o", "    68\t\r\n    69\t#### `detect`\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\tRun all anomaly detection rules (defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`) across the evidence:\r\n    72\t- Timeline-based anomalies (from log shards)\r\n    73\t- Checkpoint integrity anomalies (from .mlck files)\r\n    74\t- Cross-artifact anomalies (correlating checkpoints with logs)\r\n    75\t\r\n"]
[7802.820847, "o", "    76\tEvery anomaly object includes a top-level `evidence` field. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values` with up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies have an empty `evidence` object.\r\n    77\t\r\n    78\tDetect-specific flags:\r\n    79\t- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.\r\n    80\t- `--filter-severity LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the specified severity level or above. Severity order is `critical > high > medium > low > info`. For example, `--filter-severity high` shows only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--filter-severity c"]
[7802.820957, "o", "ritical` shows only `critical` anomalies. The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n    83\t\r\n    84\t#### `lineage`\r\n    85\t\r\n    86\tBuild a directed acyclic graph of model checkpoint relationships using the `parent_hash` field from each checkpoint's provenance section.\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\t**Rules**:\r\n    89\t- Each checkpoint is a node identified by its SHA-256 file hash\r\n    90\t- An edge `A -> B` exists if B's `parent_hash` matches A's file hash\r\n    91\t- Root nodes have empty `parent_hash`\r\n    92\t- Orphan nodes reference a parent not present in the evidence set\r\n    93\t- If a cycle is detected, report it as an anomaly (the graph should be a DAG)\r\n    94\t\r\n    95\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\"."]
[7802.821025, "o", "\r\n    96\t\r\n    97\t#### `query`\r\n    98\t\r\n    99\t```\r\n   100\tmlforge query <evidence-dir> \"<expression>\"\r\n   101\t```\r\n   102\t\r\n   103\tFilter the unified timeline using the query expression language defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md` section \"Query Language\".\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\tOutput (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n"]
[7802.821115, "o", "   106\t\r\n   107\t#### `diff`\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t```\r\n   110\tmlforge diff <evidence-dir> <file1> <file2>\r\n   111\t```\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\tCompare two checkpoint files inside `<evidence-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<evidence-dir>`.\r\n   114\t\r\n   115\tFor every tensor name present in either file, include one entry in `tensor_diffs`, sorted by tensor name lexicographically. `max_abs_diff` and `mean_abs_diff` are included only when both files contain the tensor and their shapes match.\r\n   116\t\r\n   117\tIf either checkpoint filename does not exist under `<evidence-dir>`, exit non-zero and print an error to stderr.\r\n"]
[7802.821182, "o", "   118\t\r\n   119\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Diff Output\".\r\n   120\t\r\n   121\t#### `report`\r\n   122\t\r\n   123\tGenerate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results.\r\n   124\t\r\n   125\tOutput (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n   126\t\r\n   127\t## Exit Codes\r\n   128\t\r\n   129\t| Code | Meaning |\r\n"]
[7802.821268, "o", "   130\t|------|---------|\r\n   131\t| 0 | Success |\r\n   132\t| 1 | Input error (missing directory, no artifacts, invalid arguments) |\r\n   133\t| 2 | Parse error (corrupt or unreadable artifact) |\r\n   134\t\r\n   135\tWhen a parse error occurs for individual artifacts within a batch operation (e.g., one corrupt checkpoint among several), the tool should continue processing remaining artifacts, report the error in the output, and exit with code 0. Exit code 2 is only for cases where the error prevents any meaningful output.\r\n   136\t\r\n   137\t## Build\r\n   138\t\r\n   139\t```bash\r\n   140\tcd /app && go build -o mlforge ./cmd/mlforge\r\n   141\t```\r\n   142\t\r\n"]
[7802.821345, "o", "   143\t## Cross-References\r\n   144\t\r\n   145\t- Binary formats: `/app/docs/formats.md`\r\n   146\t- Detection algorithms and query language: `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`\r\n   147\t- JSON output schemas: `/app/docs/output_schema.md`\r\n"]
