[7830.758599, "o", "3:## Overview\r\n7:## CLI Interface\r\n15:### Commands\r\n27:### Global Flags\r\n31:| `--format` | string | `json` | Output format: `json`, `text`, or `csv` (`csv` is supported only by `detect`) |\r\n34:### Command-Specific Behavior\r\n36:#### `ingest`\r\n43:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Ingest Output\".\r\n47:#### `timeline`\r\n56:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Timeline Output\".\r\n58:#### `verify`\r\n67:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Verify Output\".\r\n69:#### `detect`\r\n79:- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.\r\n80:- `--filter-severity LEVEL`: filter anomalies to show only those at the specified severity level or above. Severity order is `critical > high > medium > low > info`. For example, `--filter-severity high` shows "]
[7830.758788, "o", "only `critical` and `high` anomalies, while `--filter-severity critical` shows only `critical` anomalies. The returned JSON summary reflects the filtered anomaly list.\r\n82:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Detect Output\".\r\n84:#### `lineage`\r\n95:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Lineage Output\".\r\n97:#### `query`\r\n105:Output (JSON to stdout): list of matching timeline entries.\r\n107:#### `diff`\r\n113:Compare two checkpoint files inside `<evidence-dir>` tensor by tensor and write JSON to stdout. `file1` and `file2` are checkpoint filenames relative to `<evidence-dir>`.\r\n119:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Diff Output\".\r\n121:#### `report`\r\n125:Output (JSON to stdout): see `/app/docs/output_schema.md` section \"Report Output\".\r\n127:## Exit Codes\r\n137:## Build\r\n143:## Cross-References\r\n147:- JSON output schemas: `/app/docs/output_schema.md`\r\n"]
[7830.759054, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[7830.759145, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[7870.350325, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('docs/output_schema.md')\ns = p.read_text()\n\n# Insert metadata contract after intro.\nold = \"All commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\\n\\n---\"\nnew = \"\"\"All commands output JSON to stdout. This document defines the exact JSON structure for each command.\n\n## Execution Metadata\n\nEvery JSON command output includes a top-level `metadata` object alongside the command-specific fields. The metadata object is not added to CSV output.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"command\": \"detect\",\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/tmp/test_evidence\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nField requirements:\n\n- `tool`: always `\"mlforge\"`.\n- `version`: always `\"1.0\"`.\n- `command`: the subcommand name, such as `\"ingest\"`, `\"timeline\"`, `\"verify\"`, `\"detect\"`, `\"lineage\"`, `\"query\"`, `\"diff\"`, or `\"report\"`.\n- `evidence_dir`: the evidence directory path passed to the command.\n- `time"]
[7870.350637, "i", "stamp`: the command execution time as an ISO 8601 / RFC3339 UTC timestamp.\n\nThe examples below show `metadata` with placeholder values. Actual timestamps are generated at execution time.\n\n---\"\"\"\nif old not in s:\n    raise ValueError('intro not found')\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Ingest Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n  \"artifacts\": {', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"ingest\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n  \"artifacts\": {', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Timeline Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"total_entries\": 1200,', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"timeline\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"total_entries\": 1200,', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Ve"]
[7870.350735, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[7870.350837, "i", "rify Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"checkpoints\": [', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"verify\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"checkpoints\": [', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Detect Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"anomalies\": [', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"detect\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"anomalies\": [', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Lineage Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"nodes\": [', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"lineage\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"nodes\": [', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Query Output example if present; otherwise generic insertion after status.\ns = s.replace('\"s"]
[7870.350877, "o", "stamp`: the command execution time as an ISO 8601 / RFC3339 UTC timestamp.\r\n\r\nThe examples below show `metadata` with placeholder values. Actual timestamps are generated at execution time.\r\n\r\n---\"\"\"\r\nif old not in s:\r\n    raise ValueError('intro not found')\r\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\r\n\r\n# Add metadata to Ingest Output example.\r\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n  "]
[7870.351047, "i", "tatus\": \"ok\",\\n  \"query\":', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"query\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"query\":', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Diff Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"file_a\":', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"diff\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\\n  \"file_a\":', 1)\n\n# Add metadata to Report Output example.\ns = s.replace('\"version\": \"1.0\",\\n  \"generated_at\":', '\"metadata\": {\\n    \"tool\": \"mlforge\",\\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n    \"command\": \"report\",\\n    \"evidence_dir\": \"/path/to/evidence\",\\n    \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00Z\"\\n  },\\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\\n  \"generated_at\":', 1)\n\np.write_text(s)\nPY\n"]
