[7948.302693, "o", "docs/output_schema.md:7:Every JSON command output includes a top-level `metadata` object alongside the command-specific fields. The metadata object is not added to CSV output.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:11:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:29:The examples below show `metadata` with placeholder values. Actual timestamps are generated at execution time.\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:37:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:53:        \"num_metadata\": 3,\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:105:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:158:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:208:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:298:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:350:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:380:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/output_schema.md:417:  \"metadata\": {\r\ndocs/spec.md:9:All commands write JSON to stdout unless otherwise specified. Every JSON command output includes a top-level `metadata` object with `tool`, `version`, `command`, `evidence_dir`, and `timestamp` fields. CSV output is not modified and does not include JSON me"]
[7948.302877, "o", "tadata.\r\ndocs/spec.md:81:- `--format csv`: output CSV instead of JSON. CSV output remains CSV-only and does not include a JSON `metadata` object. The CSV header is exactly `id,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint`; one data row is emitted per anomaly. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field.\r\ndocs/spec.md:125:Generate a comprehensive forensic report by running all analyses (ingest, timeline, verify, detect, lineage) and combining results. The report output includes top-level metadata with `command: \"report\"`; nested report sections do not include their own metadata objects.\r\n"]
[7948.303128, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[7948.303198, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[7953.523635, "i", "\n"]
[7953.523965, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[7995.65605, "i", "tmpdir=$(mktemp -d)\nprintf '{\"model_name\":\"test-model\",\"dataset\":\"test-dataset\"}\\n' > \"$tmpdir/config_train.json\"\n./mlforge ingest \"$tmpdir\" | tee /tmp/ingest.json | python3 -m json.tool >/dev/null && grep -q '\"metadata\"' /tmp/ingest.json && grep -q '\"command\": \"ingest\"' /tmp/ingest.json\n./mlforge report \"$tmpdir\" | tee /tmp/report.json | python3 -m json.tool >/dev/null && grep -q '\"command\": \"report\"' /tmp/report.json && ! grep -q '\"metadata\"' <(./mlforge report \"$tmpdir\" | python3 -c 'import sys,json; r=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(r[\"ingest\"]))')\n./mlforge detect --format=json \"$tmpdir\" | tee /tmp/detect.json | python3 -m json.tool >/dev/null && grep -q '\"command\": \"detect\"' /tmp/detect.json\n./mlforge detect --format=csv \"$tmpdir\" | head -n 1\nrm -rf \"$tmpdir\"\n"]
[7995.656323, "o", "tmpdir=$(mktemp -d)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[7995.65992, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
